a rollover.\"),\n    formality='', cond_level='',\n    why=(\"Stated revision/extension of the round's final solicitation (not a new round). Requested by the target side; reason \"\n         \"stated. New due date in the structured field.\"),\n    quotes=[q(\"the ad hoc committee instructed J.P. Morgan to inform each bidder that it would need to increase its bid, and to instruct the bidders to submit improved bids on December 12, 2014.\", 25)],\n    src=['P-026'], main='P-026', review='Q6', count=None,\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,10), dto=D(2014,12,10), wdate=D(2014,12,10), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\n    conddetail=None, duedate=D(2014,12,12), dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\n    page=25, related='R034; R040; R041', deal='petsmart')\n\n# R040\nadd(when='12/12/2014 (evening)', who='PetSmart / bidders', what='Deadline', process=1, round='3', type='',\n    terms=(\"Improved-bid deadline reached. Bidder 2 submitted $81.50 per share in cash and confirmed through J.P. Morgan that \"\n           \"it was its best and final offer; the Buyer Group submitted $83.00 per share in cash as its best and final offer \"\n           \"(after an interim oral $82.50). Treatment: Enforced — the board took its next step (approval of the Buyer Group on \"\n           \"12/13/2014) on the bids in hand.\"),\n    formality='', cond_level='',\n    why=(\"Stated milestone; treatment per what followed in the round.\"),\n    quotes=[q(\"During the evening of December 12, 2014, Bidder 2 submitted an offer of $81.50 per share, in cash.\", 26)],\n    src=['P-029'], main='P-029', review='Q6', count=None,\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,12), dto=D(2014,12,12), wdate=D(2014,12,12), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\n    conddetail=None, duedate=D(2014,12,12), dtreat='Enforced', rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\n    page=26, related='R039; R042; R043; R044; R045', deal='petsmart')\n\n# R041\nadd(when='12/12/2014 (approval and confidentiality agreement; 12/09 introductory meetings)',\n    who='Longview; Buyer Group; ad hoc committee', what='Material process update', process=1, round='3', type='',\n    terms=(\"Support: Longview (rollover) — Longview rollover/voting support formed: J.P. Morgan arranged introductory meetings \"\n           \"between Longview and the Buyer Group and between Longview and Bidder 2 on 12/09 (attended by J.P. Morgan and \"\n           \"Wachtell Lipton; bidders prohibited from disclosing intended bid prices to Longview). Early on 12/12 the Buyer Group \"\n           \"requested permission to work more closely with Longview, saying Longview participation might help it achieve a \"\n           \"higher price; the ad hoc committee approved, and later that day Longview and the Buyer Group entered a \"\n           \"confidentiality agreement permitting exchange of detailed information including bid price. Wachtell Lipton was \"\n           \"instructed to provide a voting-agreement form to Longview. The rollover and voting agreements were executed 12/14 \"\n           \"(R047). Bidder 2 said a rollover accommodation would not affect its price and would be considered only after a \"\n           \"definitive agreement.\"),\n    formality='', cond_level='',\n    why=(\"Stated support formation (at most one formation row per instruction §4). Working date = the dated approval day. \"\n         \"Longview is a rolling-over shareholder, not a bidding-unit member (no membership change).\"),\n    quotes=[q(\"Early in the day on December 12, 2014, the Buyer Group requested permission to work more closely with Longview in order to include a rollover of a portion of the Company shares managed by Longview in the Buyer Group’s bid. The Buyer Group informed J.P. Morgan that the Buyer Group was working to achieve a higher price, and that Longview participation with the Buyer Group might enhance the Buyer Group’s ability to do so.\", 25),\n            q(\"After consultation with the Company’s financial and legal advisors, the ad hoc committee approved the Buyer Group’s request, and, later that day, Longview and the Buyer Group entered into a confidentiality agreement permitting the exchange of detailed information between them, including bid price, which had not previously been shared with Longview.\", 25)],\n    src=['P-027','P-028','P-024','XROLL','XVOTE'], main='P-027', review='Q7', count=None,\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,12), dto=D(2014,12,12), wdate=D(2014,12,12), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\n    page=25, related='R042; R043; R044; R047', deal='petsmart')\n\n# R042\nadd(when='12/12/2014 (evening)', who='Bidder 2', what='Bid', process=1, round='3', type='Financial',\n    terms=(\"Improved and best-and-final offer: $81.50 per share, in cash; J.P. Morgan confirmed by conversation on 12/12 that \"\n           \"$81.50 was Bidder 2's best and final offer. It also submitted a revised draft of the merger agreement and other \"\n           \"transaction agreements and financing commitment documents.\"),\n    formality='Formal', cond_level='Light',\n    why=(\"Formality: returned revised transaction documents and financing commitments responding to the best-and-final \"\n         \"solicitation (signals 1–2). Conditions: Light — committed financing documented and no Heavy trigger reported.\"),\n    quotes=[q(\"During the evening of December 12, 2014, Bidder 2 submitted an offer of $81.50 per share, in cash. Representatives of J.P. Morgan confirmed via a conversation with Bidder 2 on the evening of December 12, 2014 that $81.50 per share was its best and final offer.\", 26),\n            q(\"In addition, each bidder submitted a revised draft of the merger agreement and other transaction agreements, and copies of their respective financing commitment documents.\", 26)],\n    src=['P-029'], main='P-029', review='Q4', count=0,\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,12), dto=D(2014,12,12), wdate=D(2014,12,12), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\n    plow=81.50, phigh=81.50, pkind='Point', porigin='Stated', ccy='USD', allcash='Yes', cashclose=81.50,\n    conddetail='Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: not disclosed; Excl: not stated',\n    duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\n    page=26, related='R036; R046', deal='petsmart')\n\n# R043\nadd(when='12/12/2014 (evening)', who='Buyer Group', what='Bid', process=1, round='3', type='Financial',\n    terms=(\"Interim oral offer: $82.50 per share, in cash, with a statement that the Buyer Group was working to increase the \"\n           \"offer within the next few hours; superseded later the same evening by the $83.00 best-and-final offer (R044). \"\n           \"Preserved as made; not retrospectively upgraded.\"),\n    formality='Formal', cond_level='Light',\n    why=(\"Stated interim oral offer. Formality carried forward from the Buyer Group's formal documentation established in the \"\n         \"final-bid stage (continuing proposal); Conditions Light as at R044.\"),\n    quotes=[q(\"The Buyer Group initially submitted an oral offer of $82.50 per share, in cash, but stated that it was working to increase the offer within the next few hours.\", 26),\n            q(\"the Buyer Group informed representatives of the Company that after increasing its offer from $82.50 to $83.00 per share, some members of the group, or all of them, were unwilling or unable to offer additional consideration.\", 27)],\n    src=['P-029','XPROC'], main='P-029', review='Q4', count=0,\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,12), dto=D(2014,12,12), wdate=D(2014,12,12), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\n    plow=82.50, phigh=82.50, pkind='Point', porigin='Stated', ccy='USD', allcash='Yes', cashclose=82.50,\n    conddetail='Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: not disclosed; Excl: not stated',\n    duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\n    page=26, related='R035; R044', deal='petsmart')\n\n# R044\nadd(when='12/12/2014 (evening)', who='Buyer Group', what='Bid', process=1, round='3', type='Financial',\n    terms=(\"Best-and-final offer: $83.00 per share, in cash; submitted with a revised draft of the merger agreement and other \"\n           \"transaction agreements and copies of financing commitment documents. The Buyer Group's versions were, with few \"\n           \"exceptions, in substantially executable form; after raising from $82.50 some or all members were unwilling or \"\n           \"unable to offer more, and Longview's participation with respect to $250 million of common stock was helpful to \"\n           \"achieving $83.00.\"),\n    formality='Formal', cond_level='Light',\n    why=(\"Formality: substantially executable returned agreement and financing commitments responding to the best-and-final \"\n         \"solicitation (signals 1–2). Conditions: committed financing, no reported diligence/financing contingency — Light; \"\n         \"no Heavy trigger. Consideration all cash for cashed-out shares (rollover explained separately).\"),\n    quotes=[q(\"Later in the evening, the Buyer Group submitted a best and final offer of $83.00 per share, in cash.\", 26),\n            q(\"The versions submitted by the Buyer Group were, with few exceptions, in substantially executable form.\", 26),\n            q(\"The Buyer Group also informed representatives of the Company that Longview’s willingness to participate in the Buyer Group with respect to $250 million of the common stock was helpful in achieving an $83.00 per share price.\", 27)],\n    src=['P-029','XPROC'], main='P-029', review='Q4', count=0,\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,12), dto=D(2014,12,12), wdate=D(2014,12,12), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\n    plow=83.00, phigh=83.00, pkind='Point', porigin='Stated', ccy='USD', allcash='Yes', cashclose=83.00,\n    conddetail='Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: not disclosed; Excl: not stated',\n    duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\n    page=26, related='R035; R043; R047', deal='petsmart')\n\n# R045\nadd(when='12/13/2014', who='PetSmart board', what='Target decision', process=1, round='3', type='',\n    terms=(\"Board reviewed the final bids and the proposed transaction; J.P. Morgan rendered its oral fairness opinion \"\n           \"(subsequently confirmed in writing) that the $83.00 per share cash consideration was fair from a financial point \"\n           \"of view; the board unanimously determined the merger advisable and in the best interests of PetSmart and its \"\n           \"stockholders and resolved to recommend approval, subject to confirmation that the remaining open points in the \"\n           \"merger agreement had been satisfactorily resolved. The board could reconvene if the ad hoc committee or chairman \"\n           \"deemed necessary.\"),\n    formality='', cond_level='',\n    why=(\"Stated approval/selection decision; the winning bidder and price identified. Ordinary fairness/approval details folded \"\n         \"in because their timing and qualifications are material.\"),\n    quotes=[q(\"Following extensive discussion, the board unanimously determined that the merger agreement and the transactions contemplated thereby, including the merger, were advisable and in the best interests of PetSmart and its stockholders, and to recommend that the Company’s stockholders approve the adoption of the merger agreement. The board’s determination was subject, however, to confirmation that the remaining open points in the merger agreement had been satisfactorily resolved\", 26)],\n    src=['P-030'], main='P-030', review='', count=None,\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,13), dto=D(2014,12,13), wdate=D(2014,12,13), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\n    page=26, related='R044; R046; R047', deal='petsmart')\n\n# R046\nadd(when='12/14/2014 (Buyer Group selected 12/13/2014; agreement signed 12/14/2014)',\n    who='Bidder 2', what='Not selected at signing', process=1, round='3', type='Financial',\n    terms=(\"Bidder 2 remained live through its $81.50 best-and-final offer; the target negotiated with two other bidding \"\n           \"groups but neither was willing to make a definitive offer above $81.50, and the board chose the Buyer Group's \"\n           \"$83.00. Outcome basis Stated (the filing reports the negotiation outcome and Bidder 2's best-and-final price).\"),\n    formality='', cond_level='',\n    why=(\"Stated outcome: still bidding when the target chose another bidder; no earlier withdrawal. Decided by Target; reason: \"\n         \"lower offer than the winning bid.\"),\n    quotes=[q(\"ultimately negotiated with the Buyer Group as well as two other bidding groups, neither of which was willing to make a definitive offer at a price above $81.50, which was lower than the $83.00 price offered by the Buyer Group. The board noted that Bidder 2 had informed the Company’s representatives that $81.50 per share was its best and final offer.\", 27)],\n    src=['XPROC','P-031'], main='XPROC', review='Q2', count=1,\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,14), dto=D(2014,12,14), wdate=D(2014,12,14), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby='Target', exitreason='Lower offer than rivals', obasis='Stated',\n    page=27, related='R042; R047', deal='petsmart')\n\n# R047\nadd(when='12/14/2014', who='PetSmart; Argos Holdings Inc. (Parent); Argos Merger Sub Inc.', what='Merger agreement signed',\n    process=1, round='3', type='',\n    terms=(\"Support: Longview (rollover) — Agreed consideration $83.00 per share in cash for each outstanding share (other than \"\n           \"excluded/appraisal shares). Longview contributes 3,012,050 shares (≈$250 million worth) to Parent immediately before \"\n           \"the effective time for equity interests and receives $83.00 on its other shares; the voting agreement covers \"\n           \"7,424,591 shares. The merger is not subject to a financing condition; committed cash equity up to ~$1.83 billion \"\n           \"and committed debt up to $6.95 billion ($4.3bn term loan B, $750m ABL, $1.9bn bridge/notes), with ~$425 million \"\n           \"cash on hand and total funds of ~$8.4 billion. Termination fees $255 million (Company) / $510 million (Parent, \"\n           \"several Buyer Group termination-fee commitments); end date 06/14/2015. No go-shop; the 15 signers' standstills \"\n           \"limit post-signing bids.\"),\n    formality='', cond_level='',\n    why=(\"Stated execution of the merger agreement, voting agreement and related transaction agreements (signing is not an extra \"\n         \"submitted bid; structured bid-price and formality/conditionality fields intentionally blank). Consideration and \"\n         \"support terms stated; per-share price for cash consideration.\"),\n    quotes=[q(\"On December 14, 2014, the parties executed the merger agreement, the voting agreement and related transaction agreements and issued a press release announcing the transaction.\", 26),\n            q(\"Under the voting agreement, Longview agreed, among other things, to vote or cause to be voted 7,424,591 shares of common stock, which represent approximately 7.5% of the total outstanding shares of common stock as of the close of business on the record date, in favor of the adoption of the merger agreement\", 45),\n            q(\"Longview has agreed to contribute 3,012,050 shares (“rollover shares”) to Parent immediately prior to the effective time in exchange for equity interests in Parent.\", 41)],\n    src=['P-031','XVOTE','XROLL','XFIN','XNOFIN','XCTF','XPTF'], main='P-031', review='', count=None,\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,14), dto=D(2014,12,14), wdate=D(2014,12,14), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\n    page=26, related='R041; R044; R045; R046; R048', deal='petsmart')\n\n# R048\nadd(when='12/14/2014', who='PetSmart; Parent', what='Merger announced', process=1, round='3', type='',\n    terms=(\"Press release issued announcing the transaction, together with execution of the merger agreement, voting agreement \"\n           \"and related transaction agreements.\"),\n    formality='', cond_level='',\n    why=(\"Stated publicity; kept separate from signing and closing.\"),\n    quotes=[q(\"and issued a press release announcing the transaction.\", 26)],\n    src=['P-031'], main='P-031', review='', count=None,\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,14), dto=D(2014,12,14), wdate=D(2014,12,14), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\n    page=26, related='R047', deal='petsmart')\n\n# R049\nadd(when='by 01/29/2015 (record date; retention date not disclosed)', who='Innisfree M&A Incorporated',\n    what='Adviser engaged', process=1, round='post', type='',\n    terms=(\"Proxy solicitation firm retained to assist with the special-meeting solicitation; approximately $182,725 paid as of \"\n           \"the 01/29/2015 record date and approximately $240,000 expected in total through March 2015. Other adviser \"\n           \"relationships (engagement date not disclosed).\"),\n    formality='', cond_level='',\n    why=(\"Stated retention and fees. Included as a disclosed adviser; Working date = 01/29/2015 upper bound (assigned; retention \"\n         \"date undisclosed).\"),\n    quotes=[q(\"Innisfree M&A Incorporated, a proxy solicitation firm, has been retained to assist it in the solicitation of proxies for the special meeting. As of the record date, the Company has paid Innisfree M&A Incorporated approximately $182,725 for the solicitation of proxies in connection with the special meeting and other advisory work, and expects to pay Innisfree M&A Incorporated, in the aggregate, approximately $240,000 through March 2015.\", 20)],\n    src=['XINN'], main='XINN', review='Q7', count=None,\n    dfrom=None, dto=D(2015,1,29), wdate=D(2015,1,29), basis='Relative only', method='Assigned: bound',\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\n    page=20, related='', deal='petsmart')\n\n# Assign # and Row ids\nfor i, r in enumerate(LA, start=1):\n    r['num'] = i\n    r['rid'] = f'R{i:03d}'\n\nprint('rows:', len(LA))\njson.dump(LA, open('/tmp/opencode/petsmart/ledger_draft.json','w'), ensure_ascii=False, default=str, indent=1)\njson.dump(src_rows, open('/tmp/opencode/petsmart/source_rows.json','w'), ensure_ascii=False, indent=1)\nprint('done')\n","path":"/tmp/opencode/petsmart/build_data.py"},"output":"Created file successfully: /tmp/opencode/petsmart/build_data.py","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: /tmp/opencode/petsmart/build_data.py"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Build petsmart ledger workbook from the instruction's schema.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport datetime as dt\\nimport json, re\\nfrom openpyxl import Workbook\\nfrom openpyxl.styles import Font, Alignment, PatternFill, Border, Side\\nfrom openpyxl.utils import get_column_letter\\nfrom openpyxl.worksheet.datavalidation import DataValidation\\nfrom openpyxl.workbook.defined_name import DefinedName\\nfrom utils import page_blocks\\n\\nD = dt.date\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# 1. Source text rows\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nP = json.load(open('/tmp/opencode/petsmart/source_P.json'))\\n\\nXPASS = [\\n    ('XBG',    1,  'the “Buyer Group” refers to a consortium'),\\n    ('XEFF',   2,  'The merger agreement provides that at the effective time of the merger each outstanding share'),\\n    ('XOWN',   2,  'Following the merger, the Company will therefore become a privately held company'),\\n    ('XSH',    2,  'As of the close of business on the record date, there were 99,455,151 shares'),\\n    ('XCLOSE', 3,  'We anticipate completing the merger in the first half of 2015'),\\n    ('XCOND',  3,  'Each party’s obligation to complete the merger is subject to the satisfaction or waiver of the following conditions'),\\n    ('XFIN',   5,  'Parent estimates that the total amount required'),\\n    ('XNOFIN', 5,  'The consummation of the merger is not subject to a financing condition'),\\n    ('XTFC',   5,  'Each of the members of the Buyer Group (other than Longview) has entered into a termination fee commitment letter'),\\n    ('XHSR',   6,  'On December 24, 2014, both the Company and Parent filed'),\\n    ('XNOSOL', 6,  'But if, prior to obtaining the required vote'),\\n    ('XTERN',  7,  'the effective time of the merger has not occurred on or before June 14, 2015'),\\n    ('XCTF',   8,  'The Company will pay to Parent a termination fee of $255 million'),\\n    ('XPTF',   8,  'Parent will pay to the Company a reverse termination fee of $510 million'),\\n    ('XEXP',   8,  'then the Company will be required to reimburse Parent for all reasonable'),\\n    ('XPS',   16,  'PetSmart, Inc. is a Delaware corporation with principal executive offices'),\\n    ('XARG',  16,  'Argos Holdings Inc. is a Delaware corporation. Argos Merger Sub Inc. is a Delaware corporation'),\\n    ('XINN',  20,  'Innisfree M&A Incorporated, a proxy solicitation firm, has been retained'),\\n    ('XPREM', 26,  'a premium of 38.8%'),\\n    ('XPROC', 27,  'contacted or were contacted by more than 25 potential participants'),\\n    ('XSTAND',28,  'standstill provisions that prevent those parties from submitting'),\\n    ('XNOOFF',28,  'no person has made an unsolicited offer'),\\n    ('XLV',   29,  'managed 9% of the Company’s outstanding stock'),\\n    ('XENG',  30,  'Pursuant to an engagement letter effective as of August 21, 2014'),\\n    ('XMKT',  33,  'closing share price of $78.82 on December 9, 2014'),\\n    ('XDCF',  35,  'implied per share equity value range for shares of the Company’s common stock, rounded to the nearest $0.25, of $78.25'),\\n    ('XND',   35,  'assuming estimated net debt / (cash) of $91 million'),\\n    ('XFEE',  37,  'an amount up to approximately $39 million'),\\n    ('XREL',  37,  'received compensation or other financial benefits from the members of the Buyer Group'),\\n    ('XPROJ', 37,  'Following the release of the Company’s third fiscal quarter financial results'),\\n    ('XEQ',   40,  'entered into equity commitment letters'),\\n    ('XROLL', 41,  'Longview has agreed to contribute 3,012,050 shares'),\\n    ('XLVS',  41,  'Longview will receive the same $83.00 per share'),\\n    ('XDEBT', 41,  'in the aggregate up to $6.95 billion'),\\n    ('XTFC2', 44,  'have also executed and delivered a termination fee commitment letter'),\\n    ('XVOTE', 45,  'On December 14, 2014, the Company entered into the voting agreement'),\\n    ('XLIT',  52,  'seven putative class action lawsuits'),\\n]\\n\\nX = []\\nfor k, pg, needle in XPASS:\\n    hits = [b[2] for b in page_blocks(pg) if needle.lower() in b[2].lower()]\\n    if not hits:\\n        raise SystemExit(f'X passage not found: {k} p{pg} {needle}')\\n    X.append({'key': k, 'section': None, 'page': pg, 'text': hits[0]})\\n\\n# sections for X\\nXSEC = {\\n 'XBG':'Summary','XEFF':'Summary','XOWN':'Summary','XSH':'Summary','XCLOSE':'Summary',\\n 'XCOND':'Summary','XFIN':'Summary','XNOFIN':'Summary','XTFC':'Summary','XHSR':'Summary',\\n 'XNOSOL':'Summary','XTERN':'Summary','XCTF':'Summary','XPTF':'Summary','XEXP':'Summary',\\n 'XPS':'The Parties to the Merger Agreement','XARG':'The Parties to the Merger Agreement',\\n 'XINN':'The Special Meeting','XPREM':'Reasons for the Merger','XPROC':'Reasons for the Merger',\\n 'XSTAND':'Reasons for the Merger','XNOOFF':'Reasons for the Merger','XLV':'Reasons for the Merger',\\n 'XENG':'Opinion of J.P. Morgan','XMKT':'Opinion of J.P. Morgan','XDCF':'Opinion of J.P. Morgan',\\n 'XND':'Opinion of J.P. Morgan','XFEE':'Opinion of J.P. Morgan','XREL':'Opinion of J.P. Morgan',\\n 'XPROJ':'Projected Financial Information','XEQ':'Financing','XROLL':'Financing','XLVS':'Financing',\\n 'XDEBT':'Financing','XTFC2':'Termination Fee Commitment Letters','XVOTE':'Voting Support Agreement',\\n 'XLIT':'Litigation',\\n}\\nfor x in X:\\n    x['section'] = XSEC[x['key']]\\n\\n# Assign ids: P-001.. then X-001.. in page order (X list is already page-ordered)\\nfor i, x in enumerate(X):\\n    x['id'] = f'X-{i+1:03d}'\\n\\nXID = {x['key']: x['id'] for x in X}\\n\\nsrc_rows = []\\nfor p in P:\\n    src_rows.append({'id': p['id'], 'section': p['section'], 'page': p['page'], 'text': p['text']})\\nfor x in X:\\n    src_rows.append({'id': x['id'], 'section': x['section'], 'page': x['page'], 'text': x['text']})\\n\\ndef pg_of(ref):\\n    for p in P:\\n        if p['id'] == ref:\\n            return p['page']\\n    for x in X:\\n        if x['id'] == ref or x.get('key') == ref:\\n            return x['page']\\n    raise KeyError(ref)\\n\\ndef id_of(ref):\\n    if re.fullmatch(r'P-\\\\d+', ref):\\n        return ref\\n    return XID[ref]\\n\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# 2. Ledger rows\\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\\ndef q(text, page):\\n    return {'text': text, 'page': page}\\n\\nLA = []  # ledger rows\\n\\ndef add(**kw):\\n    LA.append(kw)\\n\\n# R001\\nadd(when='March 2014 (board authorization); Spring 2014 (discussions)',\\n    who='PetSmart board and management (contacting Industry Participant)',\\n    what='Target interest', process=1, round='0', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"PetSmart considered a merger with or acquisition of Industry Participant, a privately-held company in its \\\"\\n           \\\"industry; the board authorized management in March 2014 to test interest, and discussions during Spring 2014 \\\"\\n           \\\"ended with Industry Participant saying it was not for sale and that antitrust clearance for a combination \\\"\\n           \\\"would be unavailable or available only with unacceptable conditions. PetSmart-side acquisition attempt — \\\"\\n           \\\"recorded as context; not a bid for PetSmart and excluded from core bid counts.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated: the filing describes PetSmart's own exploration of acquiring Industry Participant. Scope: direction is \\\"\\n         \\\"PetSmart→Industry Participant, so this is not a whole-company bid for the target; kept because it frames the \\\"\\n         \\\"later exclusion decision (R011) and the initiation story.\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"During the first calendar quarter of 2014, one of the alternatives considered by the board was a merger with or acquisition of another participant in PetSmart’s industry, a privately-held company which we refer to here as “Industry Participant.”\\\", 21),\\n            q(\\\"Industry Participant’s CEO informed Mr. Lenhardt that Industry Participant was not for sale and that, in any event, Industry Participant’s management and owners believed that antitrust clearance for a combination of PetSmart and Industry Participant would not be received or would be received only with unacceptable conditions.\\\", 21)],\\n    src=['P-002'], main='P-002', review='Q8', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,3,1), dto=D(2014,6,30), wdate=D(2014,3,1), basis='Reported interval', method='Assigned: bound',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=21, related='R011', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R002\\nadd(when='05/21/2014 (earnings release); late May–June 2014 (communications)',\\n    who='PetSmart; stockholders and interested parties',\\n    what='Material process update', process=1, round='0', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"Q1 earnings released below Wall Street expectations with weaker guidance; in late May–June the Company received \\\"\\n           \\\"written or verbal communications from some stockholders and interested parties suggesting strategic or financial \\\"\\n           \\\"alternatives, including a levered return of capital and a sale of the Company. Unpriced; initiation context.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated: initiation context after the earnings miss. No price, no participant admitted; Count blank.\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"On May 21, 2014, the Company released its first quarter earnings announcement, which disclosed quarterly performance below Wall Street expectations and weaker-than-expected guidance for its second quarter and full year. Following this release, in late May and June 2014, the Company received written or verbal communications from some stockholders and from interested parties suggesting that the Company engage in various strategic or financial alternatives. Among the alternatives suggested were a levered return of capital to stockholders and a sale of the Company.\\\", 21)],\\n    src=['P-003'], main='P-003', review='Q1', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,5,21), dto=D(2014,6,30), wdate=D(2014,5,21), basis='Reported interval', method='Assigned: bound',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=21, related='', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R003\\nadd(when='06/18/2014', who='PetSmart board', what='Target sale decision', process=1, round='0', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"Board determined to explore more intensively potential changes to the Company's capital structure, with a focus \\\"\\n           \\\"on returning capital to stockholders — a capital-structure review, not yet a decision to sell; established the \\\"\\n           \\\"ad hoc committee (Chairman Gregory Josefowicz and directors Rakesh Gangwal and Thomas Stemberg) to review \\\"\\n           \\\"alternatives and authorized vetting and retention of a financial advisor.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated; qualifications preserved (capital-return focus). Sale exploration began as one alternative among several.\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"At a meeting on June 18, 2014, the board reviewed, together with a financial advisor and with Wachtell, Lipton, Rosen & Katz (“Wachtell Lipton”), its legal advisor, the various strategic and financial alternatives potentially available to the Company and determined to explore more intensively potential changes to the Company’s capital structure, with a focus on returning capital to stockholders. The board also established an ad hoc advisory subcommittee (the “ad hoc committee”)\\\", 21),\\n            q(\\\"Chairman Gregory Josefowicz and directors Rakesh Gangwal and Thomas Stemberg, all of whom are nonexecutive, independent directors, were appointed to the ad hoc committee. In addition, the board authorized the vetting and retention of a financial advisor to assist in the review.\\\", 22)],\\n    src=['P-004','P-005'], main='P-004', review='Q1', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,6,18), dto=D(2014,6,18), wdate=D(2014,6,18), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=21, related='R004; R005', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R004\\nadd(when='06/18/2014 (first shown advising; retention date not disclosed)',\\n    who='Wachtell, Lipton, Rosen & Katz', what='Adviser service observed', process=1, round='0', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"Legal advisor to the Company; shown advising the board on strategic and financial alternatives from the 06/18/2014 \\\"\\n           \\\"meeting onward, attending board meetings and drafting/revising transaction documents through signing. Engagement \\\"\\n           \\\"date not disclosed; the filing first shows the firm acting on this mandate on 06/18/2014.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated service; first mention does not prove retention on that date. Working date = earliest date the filing shows the \\\"\\n         \\\"adviser acting on the mandate (convention).\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"the board reviewed, together with a financial advisor and with Wachtell, Lipton, Rosen & Katz (“Wachtell Lipton”), its legal advisor, the various strategic and financial alternatives potentially available to the Company\\\", 21)],\\n    src=['P-004'], main='P-004', review='Q7', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,6,18), dto=D(2014,6,18), wdate=D(2014,6,18), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=21, related='R005', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R005\\nadd(when='July 2014 (retained); engagement letter effective 08/21/2014',\\n    who='J.P. Morgan Securities LLC', what='Adviser engaged', process=1, round='0', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"Financial advisor to the Company; retained in July 2014 after interviewing several potential advisors, with an \\\"\\n           \\\"engagement letter effective 08/21/2014. Fee up to approximately $39 million with a substantial portion payable \\\"\\n           \\\"only if the merger is consummated. Disclosed relationships: J.P. Morgan and affiliates received compensation of \\\"\\n           \\\"approximately $110 million from Buyer Group members (including ~$400,000 from Longview) in the two years before \\\"\\n           \\\"its opinion; James Crown, with a significant economic interest in shares subject to the voting agreement, serves \\\"\\n           \\\"on the board of JPMorgan Chase & Co.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated engagement and fee; conflicts are the filing's own disclosures. Working date = first day of the July retention \\\"\\n         \\\"window (convention; day not disclosed); later engagement-letter date listed in Terms.\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"In July, after interviewing several potential financial advisors, the Company retained J.P. Morgan as financial advisor based on, among other factors, J.P. Morgan’s reputation, experience in mergers and acquisitions, valuation, financing and capital markets and its familiarity with the Company.\\\", 22),\\n            q(\\\"For services rendered in connection with the merger and the delivery of its opinion, the Company has agreed to pay J.P. Morgan an amount up to approximately $39 million, a substantial portion of which will become payable only if the merger is consummated.\\\", 37),\\n            q(\\\"During the two years preceding the date of its opinion, J.P. Morgan and its affiliates have received compensation or other financial benefits from the members of the Buyer Group for the foregoing services in the aggregate amount of approximately $110 million, including approximately $400,000 from Longview.\\\", 37)],\\n    src=['P-005','XENG','XFEE','XREL'], main='P-005', review='Q7', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,7,1), dto=D(2014,7,31), wdate=D(2014,7,1), basis='Reported interval', method='Assigned: bound',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=22, related='R003', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R006\\nadd(when='07/03/2014', who='JANA Partners', what='Activist pressure', process=1, round='0', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"JANA filed a Schedule 13D disclosing a 9.9% stake and an intent to engage with management and the board about a \\\"\\n           \\\"review of strategic alternatives, including a sale of the Company. Unpriced; public pressure event.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated; 9.9% stake and sale advocacy. Not a bidder (no acquisition proposal).\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"On July 3, 2014, JANA Partners filed a Schedule 13D with the SEC disclosing that JANA had acquired 9.9% of the Company’s outstanding common stock and that JANA intended to engage in discussions with management and the board with respect to a review of strategic alternatives, including a sale of the Company.\\\", 22)],\\n    src=['P-006'], main='P-006', review='', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,7,3), dto=D(2014,7,3), wdate=D(2014,7,3), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=22, related='R008', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R007\\nadd(when='07/07/2014 (public letter; May 2014 meetings and 07/10/2014 call as context)',\\n    who='Longview Asset Management, LLC', what='Activist involvement', process=1, round='0', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"Longview publicly urged the board to consider a sale of the Company and said it would consider rolling part or all \\\"\\n           \\\"of its holdings into the acquiring entity's equity (rather than cash) if doing so proved necessary to complete a \\\"\\n           \\\"transaction; it had met directors and senior management in May 2014 (business/strategy views, no specific \\\"\\n           \\\"transaction advocacy) and reiterated its advocacy in a 07/10/2014 call. Longview held roughly 9% of shares.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated; Longview is a shareholder/activist, not a bidder. The rollover willingness is the origin of the later support \\\"\\n         \\\"relationship (R041) and the voting agreement (R047).\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"On July 7, 2014, Longview made public a letter to the board in which Longview stated that the board should consider the a sale of the Company (as well as other strategic alternatives) and that should the board determine a sale transaction to be in the interests of all stockholders, Longview would consider, depending on the parties and terms involved, rolling part or all of its holdings into equity of the acquiring entity rather than receive cash consideration, should doing so prove necessary in order to enable the Company to complete a transaction.\\\", 22)],\\n    src=['P-006'], main='P-006', review='', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,7,7), dto=D(2014,7,7), wdate=D(2014,7,7), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=22, related='R041; R047', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R008\\nadd(when='07/10/2014 (meeting); July–August 2014 (amendments and letters)',\\n    who='JANA Partners', what='Activist involvement', process=1, round='0', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"JANA representatives met Company representatives in person and presented their perspectives, advocating a sale; \\\"\\n           \\\"over July and August JANA filed several Schedule 13D amendments and publicly disclosed letters to the board \\\"\\n           \\\"advocating a sale of PetSmart.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated; follows the 13D row (R006); not a bidder.\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"On July 10, 2014, representatives of JANA met in person with representatives of the Company. At this meeting, the JANA representatives presented their perspectives on the Company and advocated for a sale of the Company.\\\", 22),\\n            q(\\\"Over the course of July and August, JANA Partners filed several amendments to its Schedule 13D and publicly disclosed letters to the board, advocating for a sale of PetSmart.\\\", 22)],\\n    src=['P-006'], main='P-006', review='', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,7,10), dto=D(2014,8,31), wdate=D(2014,7,10), basis='Reported interval', method='Assigned: bound',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=22, related='R006', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R009\\nadd(when='08/07/2014', who='Industry Participant', what='Bidder interest', process=1, round='0', type='Strategic',\\n    terms=(\\\"Industry Participant's representative contacted J.P. Morgan to say that, if the Company pursued strategic \\\"\\n           \\\"alternatives, Industry Participant might be interested in re-visiting the Spring conversations about a possible \\\"\\n           \\\"combination of the two companies. Unpriced approach; reported to the ad hoc committee. Carries the first-contact \\\"\\n           \\\"fact (Count 1); Industry Participant is a strategic operating company in PetSmart's industry.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated: unpriced bidder-side approach; Scope: possible whole-company combination discussed as an alternative, but \\\"\\n         \\\"Industry Participant was never admitted to the process (see R011). Contact contribution = 1 (first-contact fact \\\"\\n         \\\"carried on this row; included in the Summary contact reconciliation explicitly).\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"On August 7, 2014, a representative of Industry Participant contacted a representative of J.P. Morgan. The Industry Participant representative indicated that she had heard rumors that J.P. Morgan was working with the Company and wanted to inform J.P. Morgan that, if the Company were to pursue strategic alternatives, Industry Participant might be interested in re-visiting the conversations that had taken place in the Spring concerning the feasibility of a possible combination of the two Companies.\\\", 22)],\\n    src=['P-007'], main='P-007', review='Q8', count=1,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,8,7), dto=D(2014,8,7), wdate=D(2014,8,7), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=22, related='R001; R011', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R010\\nadd(when='08/13/2014', who='PetSmart board', what='Target sale decision', process=1, round='0', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"Board determined to explore strategic alternatives, including a possible sale, to maximize stockholder value; \\\"\\n           \\\"instructed management to plan the Profit Improvement Plan; authorized the ad hoc committee to oversee the sale \\\"\\n           \\\"exploration and direct the Company's advisers; planned J.P. Morgan outreach to financial and strategic parties \\\"\\n           \\\"(expected in the second half of September or early October) and a public announcement of the exploration so \\\"\\n           \\\"uncontacted parties could contact J.P. Morgan.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated launch decision. The filing reports the outreach as expected weeks later, so this decision is not the round-1 \\\"\\n         \\\"anchor (R016); it is a candidate anchor listed there.\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"As a result of this meeting, the board (1) determined to explore strategic alternatives (including a possible sale of the Company) for the Company to maximize value for stockholders including by commencing a process to determine the potential value that could be achieved via a sale of the Company; (2) instructed management to commence intensive planning for a cost-reduction and profit-improvement plan (which we refer to collectively as the “Profit Improvement Plan”)\\\", 22),\\n            q(\\\"the board also considered and discussed alternative formats and timing for the conduct of the exploratory sale process, and determined that at the appropriate time, which was expected to be during the second half of September or early October, J.P. Morgan should contact financial and strategic parties deemed likely to be interested and capable of completing a transaction.\\\", 22)],\\n    src=['P-008'], main='P-008', review='Q1', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,8,13), dto=D(2014,8,13), wdate=D(2014,8,13), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=22, related='R011; R012; R016', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R011\\nadd(when='08/13/2014 (decision; communicated by telephone on 08/22/2014 and 08/27/2014)',\\n    who='PetSmart board', what='Target decision', process=1, round='0', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"Industry Participant would not be invited into the exploratory sale process. Board concerns: very high risk that \\\"\\n           \\\"a combination would not receive antitrust clearances (or only with unacceptable conditions); near-certain 'second \\\"\\n           \\\"request' and an eight-months-to-a-year delay; risk of competitive information exposure; and disruption/time-delay \\\"\\n           \\\"risk. J.P. Morgan communicated the concerns on 08/22 and 08/27; Industry Participant said it would be interested \\\"\\n           \\\"in discussing a combination; it was told it would not be invited but the board would consider any proposal it \\\"\\n           \\\"submitted. No contact since 08/27/2014 (reaffirmed 10/03/2014).\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated: target decision not to admit a party that never entered; rationale quoted. No outcome row is created because \\\"\\n         \\\"Industry Participant never entered the process (no NDA, bid or admission).\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"the board reviewed the potential benefits and risks of inviting Industry Participant to participate in the exploratory sale process. In this regard, the board considered, among other things, in addition to the communications with Industry Representative in the Spring and on August 7, the very high risk that an acquisition by or a combination with Industry Participant would not receive antitrust clearances, or would receive such clearances only with the imposition by governmental authorities of unacceptable conditions\\\", 22),\\n            q(\\\"The J.P. Morgan representative stated that Industry Participant would not be invited into the exploratory process, but that if Industry Participant were to wish to submit a proposal or other communication to the Company, the board would consider it. There has been no contact between PetSmart and Industry Participant (or between any of their respective representatives) since August 27, 2014.\\\", 23),\\n            q(\\\"the board reviewed and, for the reasons discussed in August, reaffirmed the determination not to invite Industry Participant to participate in the sale process.\\\", 23)],\\n    src=['P-008','P-009','P-010','P-012'], main='P-010', review='Q8', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,8,13), dto=D(2014,8,13), wdate=D(2014,8,13), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby='Target', exitreason=None, obasis='Stated',\\n    page=23, related='R009; R010; R015', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R012\\nadd(when='08/19/2014', who='PetSmart', what='Sale process announced', process=1, round='0', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"Press release issued concurrent with the Q2 earnings announcement: the Company determined to explore strategic \\\"\\n           \\\"alternatives to maximize stockholder value, including a possible sale. The filing says the announcement ensured \\\"\\n           \\\"interested parties not contacted would learn of the process and could contact J.P. Morgan.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated publicity of the exploration; a rejected round-1 anchor candidate (it replaced/directed outreach to inbound \\\"\\n         \\\"contact rather than launching a target outreach wave).\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"On August 19, 2014, concurrent with its second quarter earnings announcement, the Company issued a press release announcing that it determined to explore strategic alternatives for the Company to maximize value for stockholders, including a possible sale of the Company.\\\", 23)],\\n    src=['P-009'], main='P-009', review='Q1', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,8,19), dto=D(2014,8,19), wdate=D(2014,8,19), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=23, related='R010; R016', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R013 / R014 contacts\\nadd(when='mid-August through 10/03/2014 (aggregate disclosed 10/03/2014)',\\n    who='3 strategic parties (cohort; not counting Industry Participant)', what='Contact', process=1, round='0', type='Strategic',\\n    terms=(\\\"J.P. Morgan was contacted by 27 potential participants in a sale process — here the strategic component: three \\\"\\n           \\\"strategic parties, not counting Industry Participant (recorded separately at R009/R011). Aggregate contact \\\"\\n           \\\"activity, not NDA signers or bidders; none of the three signed a confidentiality agreement.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated aggregate; the filing supplies the strategic/financial split, so it is recorded as two cohort rows. Count 3 as \\\"\\n         \\\"the number of contacted strategic parties (contact tally; different step from NDA count).\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"During this period, J.P. Morgan was contacted by 27 potential participants in a sale process, including three strategic parties (not counting Industry Participant) and 24 financial participants (including potential lead buyers as well as large suppliers of equity capital to lead buyers).\\\", 23)],\\n    src=['P-011'], main='P-011', review='Q2', count=3,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,8,14), dto=D(2014,10,3), wdate=D(2014,9,8), basis='Reported interval', method='Assigned: midpoint',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=23, related='R014; R011', deal='petsmart')\\n\\nadd(when='mid-August through 10/03/2014 (aggregate disclosed 10/03/2014)',\\n    who='24 financial participants (cohort; including potential lead buyers and equity suppliers)', what='Contact',\\n    process=1, round='0', type='Financial',\\n    terms=(\\\"Financial component of the 27 contacted participants; includes potential lead buyers as well as large suppliers of \\\"\\n           \\\"equity capital to lead buyers. Aggregate contact activity; the 15 confidentiality signers are a subset of these \\\"\\n           \\\"contacts, so this row and the NDA row are not additive (different steps).\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated aggregate with filing-supplied split. Count 24 = number of contacted financial participants; overlap with the \\\"\\n         \\\"15 NDA signers noted in the reason (contacts ≠ NDA step).\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"including three strategic parties (not counting Industry Participant) and 24 financial participants (including potential lead buyers as well as large suppliers of equity capital to lead buyers).\\\", 23),\\n            q(\\\"the board was informed that approximately 15 parties had expressed interest in participating in the process.\\\", 23)],\\n    src=['P-011','P-012'], main='P-011', review='Q2', count=24,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,8,14), dto=D(2014,10,3), wdate=D(2014,9,8), basis='Reported interval', method='Assigned: midpoint',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=23, related='R013; R017', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R015\\nadd(when='10/03/2014', who='PetSmart board', what='Material process update', process=1, round='0', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"Board met for regularly scheduled business and received an update on the completed Profit Improvement Plan \\\"\\n           \\\"planning and on the sale process, including communications with the 27 potentially interested parties and \\\"\\n           \\\"Industry Participant; informed that approximately 15 parties had expressed interest in participating; \\\"\\n           \\\"reaffirmed the determination not to invite Industry Participant into the sale process.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated process update; candidate round-1 anchor rejected (it was a review/reaffirmation, not an outreach launch, \\\"\\n         \\\"and the confidentiality wave that admitted participants began the same week).\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"On October 3, 2014, the board met, together with members of management and representatives of J.P. Morgan and Wachtell Lipton, to conduct regularly scheduled business and to receive an update on the status of the Profit Improvement Plan, the planning for which had been completed, and on the sale process, including an update on communications with the 27 potentially interested parties as well as Industry Participant that had occurred since the August 13 board meeting. Among other things, the board was informed that approximately 15 parties had expressed interest in participating in the process.\\\", 23)],\\n    src=['P-012'], main='P-012', review='Q1', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,10,3), dto=D(2014,10,3), wdate=D(2014,10,3), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=23, related='R011; R016; R013; R014', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R016\\nadd(when='first week of October 2014', who='PetSmart / J.P. Morgan', what='Round opened', process=1, round='1', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"R1 anchor: confidentiality-agreement wave (first week of October 2014) — the first target-organized step that \\\"\\n           \\\"admitted participants to a stage; the filing reports no clean target-initiated outreach wave, and parties largely \\\"\\n           \\\"contacted or were contacted by J.P. Morgan / learned of the process from the 08/19 announcement. Rejected \\\"\\n           \\\"candidate anchors: Aug 13 board decision (R010), Aug 19 public announcement (R012), aggregate contacts \\\"\\n           \\\"(R013/R014), Oct 3 board meeting (R015). Round 1 purpose: confidentiality, diligence access and non-binding IOI \\\"\\n           \\\"solicitation. Round finality: Not final — no final/binding or best-and-final designation; the round closed with \\\"\\n           \\\"non-binding indications of interest.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Convention (round map): round opens under the instruction's rule 3 (no target outreach wave; first target-organized \\\"\\n         \\\"admitting step) anchored on the confidentiality wave; Working date = calendar midpoint of the first-week window \\\"\\n         \\\"(assigned).\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"In the first week of October 2014, the Company entered into confidentiality and standstill agreements with 15 potentially interested financial buyers\\\", 23)],\\n    src=['P-013'], main='P-013', review='Q1', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,10,1), dto=D(2014,10,7), wdate=D(2014,10,4), basis='Reported interval', method='Assigned: midpoint',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal='Not final', decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=23, related='R010; R012; R013; R014; R015; R017', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R017\\nadd(when='first week of October 2014 (signings); diligence during October 2014',\\n    who='15 financial buyers (cohort)', what='NDA signed', process=1, round='1', type='Financial',\\n    terms=(\\\"Company entered confidentiality and standstill agreements with 15 potentially interested financial buyers; all 15 \\\"\\n           \\\"then engaged in due diligence during October, received management presentations involving senior-most management, \\\"\\n           \\\"and received detailed financial and business-plan information including the Profit Improvement Plan. The standstills \\\"\\n           \\\"prevent the 15 from submitting (or even seeking permission to submit) a higher bid once a definitive agreement is \\\"\\n           \\\"signed; the board believed this promoted best bids. New signatures in this process; no reused coverage from an \\\"\\n           \\\"earlier attempt. Uniform stage access — any access differences are recorded at R030.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated: 15 signers, all financial buyers. Count 15 = cohort size at this step. Scope: signers did not all become \\\"\\n         \\\"bidders (see R024).\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"In the first week of October 2014, the Company entered into confidentiality and standstill agreements with 15 potentially interested financial buyers, all 15 of which, during the month of October engaged in due diligence, received management presentations involving the Company’s senior-most management, and received detailed financial and business plan information, including detailed information concerning the Profit Improvement Plan and associated cost-saving plans and opportunities.\\\", 23),\\n            q(\\\"the confidentiality agreements entered into by the 15 potentially interested parties that engaged in due diligence contained standstill provisions that prevent those parties from submitting (or even seeking permission to submit) a higher bid once the Company entered into a definitive transaction agreement with the winning sale process participant.\\\", 28)],\\n    src=['P-013','XSTAND'], main='P-013', review='Q2; Q5', count=15,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,10,1), dto=D(2014,10,7), wdate=D(2014,10,4), basis='Reported interval', method='Assigned: midpoint',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=23, related='R016; R024; R020', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R018\\nadd(when='October 2014 (communication date not disclosed)', who='PetSmart / J.P. Morgan (to the 15 potential bidders)',\\n    what='Deadline set', process=1, round='1', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"Potential bidders were informed that non-binding preliminary indications of interest would be due October 30, 2014. \\\"\\n           \\\"They were also told that Longview was willing to 'roll-over' up to 7.5 million shares on terms and price acceptable \\\"\\n           \\\"to Longview (such shares would not receive cash consideration and could remain equity) and were asked to indicate \\\"\\n           \\\"interest in Longview participation, which was not a condition to participation. Communication date within October \\\"\\n           \\\"not disclosed; known only to precede 10/30/2014.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated deadline communication plus stage information on the rollover. Working date = midpoint of the October window \\\"\\n         \\\"before the due date (assigned; order must follow the NDA row).\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"During October, the potential bidders were informed that non-binding preliminary indications of interest would be due on October 30, 2014.\\\", 23),\\n            q(\\\"The potential bidders were also informed that Longview had informed the Company that it would be willing to “roll-over” up to 7.5 million shares on terms and price acceptable to Longview, meaning that such shares would not receive cash merger consideration but would remain outstanding as equity in PetSmart or the buyer’s acquisition vehicle, if so desired by the bidder. The Company requested that, in connection with their preliminary indications of interest, the bidders should indicate their interest, if any, in participation by Longview, but that such interest was not a condition to participation in the process.\\\", 23)],\\n    src=['P-014','P-015'], main='P-014', review='Q6; Q8', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,10,1), dto=D(2014,10,29), wdate=D(2014,10,15), basis='Reported interval', method='Assigned: midpoint',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=D(2014,10,30), dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=23, related='R019; R041', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R019\\nadd(when='10/30/2014', who='PetSmart / potential bidders', what='Deadline', process=1, round='1', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"Non-binding IOI due date reached; six of the potentially interested parties submitted indications. Treatment: \\\"\\n           \\\"Enforced — the board took its next step (advancing selected bidders on 11/03/2014) on the indications in hand; no \\\"\\n           \\\"extension or late acceptance is reported.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated due-date milestone; treatment per instruction from what followed in the round.\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"On October 30, six of the potentially interested parties submitted indications of interest.\\\", 24)],\\n    src=['P-016'], main='P-016', review='Q6', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,10,30), dto=D(2014,10,30), wdate=D(2014,10,30), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=D(2014,10,30), dtreat='Enforced', rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=24, related='R018; R026', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R020\\nadd(when='10/30/2014', who='Buyer Group', what='Bid', process=1, round='1', type='Financial',\\n    terms=(\\\"Non-binding preliminary indication of interest: range of $81.00 to $83.00 per share; one of three indications \\\"\\n           \\\"reaching at least $80.00. Bid not conditioned on a Longview rollover.\\\"),\\n    formality='Informal', cond_level='Insufficient evidence',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated price range. Formality: preliminary non-binding IOI with no returned documentation signal (Informal). \\\"\\n         \\\"Conditions: the filing reports the price but nothing about this bid's financing/diligence conditions; all 15 had \\\"\\n         \\\"substantive October diligence access and further diligence followed — preferred reading noted; recorded Insufficient \\\"\\n         \\\"evidence. All cash: Not stated at IOI stage (form of consideration not disclosed).\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"Three bidders initially indicated price ranges that reached at least $80.00 per share, including the Buyer Group, which indicated a range of $81.00 to $83.00 per share\\\", 24)],\\n    src=['P-016'], main='P-016', review='Q4', count=1,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,10,30), dto=D(2014,10,30), wdate=D(2014,10,30), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=81.0, phigh=83.0, pkind='Bidder range', porigin='Stated', ccy='USD', allcash='Not stated', cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail='Fin: not stated; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: not stated',\\n    duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=24, related='R035; R043', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R021\\nadd(when='10/30/2014', who='Bidder 2', what='Bid', process=1, round='1', type='Financial',\\n    terms=(\\\"Non-binding preliminary indication of interest: initially $78.00 per share. Below the $80.00 threshold applied on \\\"\\n           \\\"11/03/2014 until revised (R025).\\\"),\\n    formality='Informal', cond_level='Insufficient evidence',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated initial price. Formality/conditions as for the other IOIs (no formal signal; financing/conditions not stated). \\\"\\n         \\\"Superseded by the revised indication before the selection decision.\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"another bidder (which we refer to as “Bidder 2”), which had initially indicated a price of $78.00\\\", 24)],\\n    src=['P-016'], main='P-016', review='Q4', count=1,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,10,30), dto=D(2014,10,30), wdate=D(2014,10,30), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=78.0, phigh=78.0, pkind='Point', porigin='Stated', ccy='USD', allcash='Not stated', cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail='Fin: not stated; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: not stated',\\n    duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=24, related='R025; R036', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R022\\nadd(when='10/30/2014', who='Unnamed bidder 1 (range $80–$85)', what='Bid', process=1, round='1', type='Financial',\\n    terms=(\\\"Non-binding preliminary indication of interest: range of $80.00 to $85.00 per share. Individually described \\\"\\n           \\\"unnamed bidder; possibly one of the two bidders that later formed Bidder 3 — identity not established (Q2), so no \\\"\\n           \\\"link is asserted in the ledger.\\\"),\\n    formality='Informal', cond_level='Insufficient evidence',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated range for an unnamed but individually distinguishable participant. No identity mapping to later anonymous \\\"\\n         \\\"roles (hypothesis only, Q2). Conditions not stated.\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"and another bidder, which suggested a range of $80.00 to $85.00 per share\\\", 24)],\\n    src=['P-016'], main='P-016', review='Q2; Q4', count=1,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,10,30), dto=D(2014,10,30), wdate=D(2014,10,30), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=80.0, phigh=85.0, pkind='Bidder range', porigin='Stated', ccy='USD', allcash='Not stated', cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail='Fin: not stated; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: not stated',\\n    duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=24, related='R028', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R023\\nadd(when='10/30/2014', who='Unnamed IOI submitters (residual cohort of 3)', what='Bid', process=1, round='1', type='Financial',\\n    terms=(\\\"Residual of the six stated IOI submitters after the three individually described indications (Buyer Group \\\"\\n           \\\"$81–$83; Bidder 2 $78; unnamed bidder $80–$85): three further submitters whose prices are not disclosed — one \\\"\\n           \\\"indicated a price or range at or above $80.00 (included within the four bidders advanced to the final round) and \\\"\\n           \\\"two were below $80.00 (eliminated on 11/03/2014). Prices and identities not disclosed.\\\"),\\n    formality='Informal', cond_level='Insufficient evidence',\\n    why=(\\\"Residual partition: 6 stated submitters − 3 individually described units = 3. Formality Informal (preliminary \\\"\\n         \\\"non-binding indications); conditions not stated. Undisclosed prices are preserved in text; no endpoints invented.\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"On October 30, six of the potentially interested parties submitted indications of interest.\\\", 24),\\n            q(\\\"The board determined to allow the four bidders that had indicated a price or range at or above $80.00 per share to proceed to the final round of the sale process.\\\", 24)],\\n    src=['P-016','P-017'], main='P-016', review='Q2; Q4', count=3,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,10,30), dto=D(2014,10,30), wdate=D(2014,10,30), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind='Undisclosed', porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash='Not stated', cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail='Fin: not stated; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: not stated',\\n    duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=24, related='R026; R028', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R024\\nadd(when='by 10/30/2014', who='9 non-submitting NDA signers (cohort)', what='Did not submit', process=1, round='1', type='Financial',\\n    terms=(\\\"Inferred: residual — 15 NDA signers − 6 submitters = 9 non-submitters. The 15 potential bidders were told IOIs \\\"\\n           \\\"were due 10/30/2014; six submitted indications and no submission is reported for the other nine. Row records only \\\"\\n           \\\"non-submission at this solicitation, not permanent withdrawal.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Inferred: residual (base assumes all 15 confidentiality signers were invited to submit and that the six stated \\\"\\n         \\\"submitters exhaust the submissions). Arithmetic in Terms. No identities, motives or decision dates inferred.\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"the potential bidders were informed that non-binding preliminary indications of interest would be due on October 30, 2014.\\\", 23),\\n            q(\\\"On October 30, six of the potentially interested parties submitted indications of interest.\\\", 24)],\\n    src=['P-014','P-016','P-013'], main='P-014', review='Q5', count=9,\\n    dfrom=None, dto=D(2014,10,30), wdate=D(2014,10,30), basis='Relative only', method='Assigned: deadline',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby='Unknown', exitreason='Not stated', obasis='Inferred: residual',\\n    page=24, related='R017; R020; R021; R022; R023', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R025\\nadd(when='between 10/30/2014 and 11/02/2014', who='Bidder 2', what='Bid', process=1, round='1', type='Financial',\\n    terms=(\\\"Revised and increased indication: range of $81.00 to $84.00 per share, after discussions with J.P. Morgan, which \\\"\\n           \\\"spoke by telephone with all potentially interested parties (including non-submitters) from 10/30 to 11/02 about \\\"\\n           \\\"their price rationales.\\\"),\\n    formality='Informal', cond_level='Insufficient evidence',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated revision; supersedes R021. Formality/conditions as for the IOIs. Working date = midpoint of the discussion \\\"\\n         \\\"window (assigned; keeps the revision ahead of the 11/03 selection).\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"As a result of its discussions with J.P. Morgan, another bidder (which we refer to as “Bidder 2”), which had initially indicated a price of $78.00, increased its indication to a range of $81.00 to $84.00 per share.\\\", 24)],\\n    src=['P-016'], main='P-016', review='Q2; Q6', count=0,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,10,30), dto=D(2014,11,2), wdate=D(2014,10,31), basis='Reported interval', method='Assigned: midpoint',\\n    plow=81.0, phigh=84.0, pkind='Bidder range', porigin='Stated', ccy='USD', allcash='Not stated', cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail='Fin: not stated; DD required: not stated; DD open: yes; Excl: not stated',\\n    duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=24, related='R021; R036', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R026\\nadd(when='11/03/2014', who='PetSmart board', what='Round opened', process=1, round='2', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"R2 opens: board met and allowed the four bidders that had indicated a price or range at or above $80.00 per share \\\"\\n           \\\"to proceed to the 'final round of the sale process'. Individually described ≥$80 units: Buyer Group (R020), Bidder 2 \\\"\\n           \\\"(R025, raised from $78) and unnamed bidder 1 (R022); one further ≥$80 submitter sits inside residual R023. Purpose: \\\"\\n           \\\"finalist diligence and negotiation toward definitive documentation. Round finality: Inferred final — selected \\\"\\n           \\\"bidders moved toward a definitive agreement; the filing calls it the board's final round, but no announcement to \\\"\\n           \\\"bidders of a binding/best-and-final stage is quoted at this opening.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated selection threshold and count; round map per instruction. See Q1/Q2 on the four-bidder composition.\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"On November 3, 2014, the board met in person, together with members of management and representatives of J.P. Morgan and Wachtell Lipton, to continue its review of strategic alternatives, including a review of the indications of interest. The board determined to allow the four bidders that had indicated a price or range at or above $80.00 per share to proceed to the final round of the sale process.\\\", 24)],\\n    src=['P-017'], main='P-017', review='Q1; Q2', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,11,3), dto=D(2014,11,3), wdate=D(2014,11,3), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal='Inferred final', decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=24, related='R020; R022; R023; R025; R027; R028; R029', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R027\\nadd(when='11/03/2014 (advancement decision; notification followed the meeting, day not disclosed)',\\n    who='2 eliminated IOI submitters (cohort)', what='Dropped by target', process=1, round='1', type='Financial',\\n    terms=(\\\"Target excluded the submitters below the ≥$80.00 threshold from the final round; J.P. Morgan notified the eliminated \\\"\\n           \\\"parties after the 11/03/2014 board meeting, and none indicated any interest or ability to remain in the process at \\\"\\n           \\\"price levels above their respective initial indications.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated exclusion of two submitting units (6 submitters − 4 advanced). Decided by Target; reason: lower price than \\\"\\n         \\\"rivals carried forward to the threshold. The notified parties' own lack of interest to remain is preserved.\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"Following this meeting, representatives of J.P. Morgan notified the eliminated parties, none of which indicated any interest or ability to remain in the process at price levels above their respective initial indications.\\\", 24)],\\n    src=['P-017','P-016'], main='P-017', review='Q2; Q5', count=2,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,11,3), dto=None, wdate=D(2014,11,3), basis='Relative only', method='Assigned: decision day',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby='Target', exitreason='Lower offer than rivals', obasis='Stated',\\n    page=24, related='R023', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R028\\nadd(when='after 11/03/2014; day not disclosed',\\n    who='Bidder 3 (two unnamed final-round bidders working together)', what='Bidding group changed', process=1, round='2', type='Financial',\\n    terms=(\\\"Two bidders — one invited into the final round that indicated a desire to work with an equity partner given the size \\\"\\n           \\\"of a PetSmart acquisition, and one that had indicated it would drop out of the process if not permitted to work \\\"\\n           \\\"together with another bidder — requested permission to work together (they had worked together successfully in \\\"\\n           \\\"prior large leveraged buyouts); the ad hoc committee authorized them, and the two are referred to together as \\\"\\n           \\\"'Bidder 3'. Effect on final-round units: 4 admitted bidders → 3 bidding units (units −1). Because the members are \\\"\\n           \\\"not independently tracked elsewhere, this row states the unit effect rather than opening per-member Joined group \\\"\\n           \\\"rows; unit arithmetic keeps the stage balance intact.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated formation and authorization. Convention: anonymous-pair treatment of the unit change (instruction §5.3); \\\"\\n         \\\"identity of members vs Unnamed bidder 1 (R022) not established (Q2).\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"Two of the bidders (one of which had been invited into the final round but had indicated a desire to work with an equity partner in light of the size of an acquisition of PetSmart, and the other of which had indicated to J.P. Morgan that it would drop out of the process if not permitted to work together with another bidder) requested permission to work together. These two bidders informed J.P. Morgan that they had worked together successfully in previous large leveraged buyouts. After deliberation and consultation with the Company’s financial and legal advisors, the ad hoc committee authorized these two bidders to work together. We refer to these two bidders together as “Bidder 3.”\\\", 24)],\\n    src=['P-018'], main='P-018', review='Q2', count=2,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,11,4), dto=None, wdate=D(2014,11,4), basis='Relative only', method='Assigned: bound',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis='Stated',\\n    page=24, related='R026; R037; R038', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R029\\nadd(when='November 2014 (day not disclosed)', who='PetSmart', what='Round opened', process=1, round='3', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"R3 anchor: first request for final bids — the Company circulated a form of merger agreement to the bidders with \\\"\\n           \\\"instructions that bidders submit any proposed comments on the merger agreement together with their final bids; \\\"\\n           \\\"bidders also engaged in further extensive due diligence and management presentations during November. Rejected \\\"\\n           \\\"candidate anchors: the 12/04–12/05 setting of the 12/10 final-bid deadline (R033/R034) — treated as deadline \\\"\\n           \\\"history inside R3, not a fresh round; the 11/03 selection (R026) opens R2. Round finality: Announced as final — \\\"\\n           \\\"bidders were instructed to deliver 'final bids' and the Company later set a 'final bids' deadline and confirmed a \\\"\\n           \\\"'best and final' offer with Bidder 2.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Round-map convention: the instruction makes the first request for final offers a new round even with unchanged \\\"\\n         \\\"bidders; the November circulation is that request. Working date = November midpoint (assigned; day not disclosed).\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"Also during November, the Company circulated a form of merger agreement to the bidders with instructions that the bidders submit any proposed comments on the merger agreement together with their final bids.\\\", 24),\\n            q(\\\"During November, the bidders engaged in further extensive due diligence investigations of the Company, including further detailed management presentations.\\\", 24)],\\n    src=['P-019'], main='P-019', review='Q1', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,11,1), dto=D(2014,11,30), wdate=D(2014,11,15), basis='Reported interval', method='Assigned: midpoint',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal='Announced as final', decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=24, related='R026; R033', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R030\\nadd(when='November 2014 (following the third-quarter earnings announcement)',\\n    who='J.P. Morgan (for PetSmart)', what='Information access changed', process=1, round='3', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"Projections updated: following release of the Company's third fiscal-quarter results, selected fiscal 2014 income \\\"\\n           \\\"statement line items were revised to reflect actual performance and better visibility into the Profit Improvement \\\"\\n           \\\"Plan; at bidders' request and the board's direction, J.P. Morgan provided bidders with updates to the fiscal 2014 \\\"\\n           \\\"projections. Access was given to the then-live (final-round) bidders; no price change.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated revision of projections after bidding began (IOIs 10/30/2014), provided to bidders — an information-access \\\"\\n         \\\"change per instruction §4. Count blank (process-wide information row).\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"Following the Company’s third quarter earnings announcement and, at the request of bidders and the direction of the board and the Company, representatives of J.P. Morgan provided the bidders with updates to the Company’s fiscal year 2014 financial projections.\\\", 24),\\n            q(\\\"Following the release of the Company’s third fiscal quarter financial results, selected income statement line items for fiscal year 2014 only were updated to reflect actual performance and better visibility into the performance of the Company’s profit improvement plan.\\\", 37)],\\n    src=['P-019','XPROJ'], main='P-019', review='Q1; Q6', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,11,1), dto=D(2014,11,30), wdate=D(2014,11,15), basis='Reported interval', method='Assigned: midpoint',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=24, related='R029', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R031\\nadd(when='12/03/2014', who='PetSmart board', what='Material process update', process=1, round='3', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"Regularly scheduled board meeting: further review and financial analysis of alternatives in light of positive \\\"\\n           \\\"operating indications from the Fall/Thanksgiving season and indications that the Profit Improvement Plan would \\\"\\n           \\\"likely achieve at least $200 million in annual incremental profit; board considered standalone values with and \\\"\\n           \\\"without a leveraged capital return. No decisions — no bids in hand. Board had initially targeted 12/15/2014 for \\\"\\n           \\\"completion and initially set 12/05/2014 for bid submissions.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated; provides the improvement rationale later cited (R039) and the original deadline plan (R032). No decisions \\\"\\n         \\\"made on the bids.\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"significant portions of this meeting were devoted to a further review and financial analysis of the Company’s strategic and financial alternatives, particularly in light of positive indications about the Company’s operating results based on preliminary information from the Fall and Thanksgiving season and indications that the Profit Improvement Plan would likely be successful in achieving at least $200 million in annual incremental profit.\\\", 24),\\n            q(\\\"The board had initially targeted Monday, December 15 for completion of the sale process, and had initially set Friday, December 5 as the date for submission of bids so as to allow sufficient time for the Company to receive and analyze the bids, conduct further rounds of bidding, if necessary, to negotiate final documentation, and to permit the winning bidder a short period of time to discuss and negotiate a Longview rollover, if desired by the winning bidder.\\\", 24)],\\n    src=['P-020'], main='P-020', review='Q1', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,3), dto=D(2014,12,3), wdate=D(2014,12,3), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=24, related='R032; R033; R039; R040', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R032\\nadd(when='reported 12/03/2014; communication date not disclosed', who='PetSmart board', what='Deadline set',\\n    process=1, round='3', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"Initial bid-submission date: Friday, December 5, 2014, set to allow analysis of bids, further bidding if needed, \\\"\\n           \\\"negotiation of final documentation and a short Longview rollover discussion by the winner; targeted completion \\\"\\n           \\\"12/15/2014. Superseded on 12/04–12/05 (R033) before it arrived, so no milestone row is recorded for 12/05.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated in the 12/03 report; exact communication date not disclosed. Upper bound = 12/03/2014 (assigned working date).\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"had initially set Friday, December 5 as the date for submission of bids\\\", 24)],\\n    src=['P-020'], main='P-020', review='Q6', count=None,\\n    dfrom=None, dto=D(2014,12,3), wdate=D(2014,12,3), basis='Relative only', method='Assigned: bound',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=D(2014,12,5), dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=24, related='R033', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R033\\nadd(when='12/04/2014 and 12/05/2014', who='Ad hoc committee', what='Deadline revised', process=1, round='3', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"Existing due date changed: from Friday 12/05/2014 to the evening of Wednesday 12/10/2014 (five days rather than \\\"\\n           \\\"ten before the anticipated 12/15 completion), to reduce the risk of leaks or unintended public disclosure; at the \\\"\\n           \\\"same time the Company asked bidders to submit mark-ups of the draft merger agreement and other transaction \\\"\\n           \\\"documents and financing commitments, if possible, in advance.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated revision; ad hoc committee conclusion over 12/04–12/05, after consultation with advisers. Old and new due \\\"\\n         \\\"dates preserved (new due date in the structured field). Working date = first day of the two-day window (assigned).\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"However, on December 4 and December 5, 2014, after consultation with the Company’s financial and legal advisors, the ad hoc committee concluded that these matters could be accomplished in a shorter period of time, which would reduce the risk of leaks or unintended public disclosure.\\\", 24),\\n            q(\\\"Accordingly, the Company set the evening of Wednesday, December 10 (five days, rather than 10 days prior to the anticipated December 15 completion date) as the deadline for submission of final bids, and at the same time asked the bidders to submit mark-ups of the draft merger agreement and the other transaction documents and financing commitments, if possible, in advance.\\\", 25)],\\n    src=['P-020','P-021'], main='P-021', review='Q6', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,4), dto=D(2014,12,5), wdate=D(2014,12,4), basis='Reported interval', method='Assigned: bound',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=D(2014,12,10), dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=25, related='R032; R034', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R034\\nadd(when='12/10/2014 (evening)', who='PetSmart / bidders', what='Deadline', process=1, round='3', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"Final-bid deadline reached. PetSmart received final bid letters with revised merger agreement and transaction \\\"\\n           \\\"documents from the Buyer Group and Bidder 2, plus a verbal indication from Bidder 3. Treatment: Extended — after \\\"\\n           \\\"reviewing the bids on 12/10 the ad hoc committee asked the same bidders to submit improved bids on 12/12/2014 \\\"\\n           \\\"(Deadline revised, R039).\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated due-date milestone; treatment Extended because the Deadline revised row R039 moves this due date.\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"On December 10, PetSmart received final bid letters along with revised versions of the merger agreement and other transaction documents from the Buyer Group and from Bidder 2 and a verbal indication from Bidder 3.\\\", 25)],\\n    src=['P-025','P-026'], main='P-025', review='Q6', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,10), dto=D(2014,12,10), wdate=D(2014,12,10), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=D(2014,12,10), dtreat='Extended', rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=25, related='R033; R035; R036; R037; R039', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R035\\nadd(when='12/10/2014', who='Buyer Group', what='Bid', process=1, round='3', type='Financial',\\n    terms=(\\\"Final bid: $80.70 per share, in cash, submitted with a revised merger agreement and other transaction documents; \\\"\\n           \\\"the Buyer Group had provided financing commitment documents on 12/06/2014. Its documentation was more favorable to \\\"\\n           \\\"the Company (less conditional, more likely to be completed, more acceptance of the Company's positions) and each \\\"\\n           \\\"bidder indicated its bid was not dependent on a Longview rollover.\\\"),\\n    formality='Formal', cond_level='Light',\\n    why=(\\\"Formality: bidder-returned revised merger agreement and transaction documents with a solicited final bid (signal 1). \\\"\\n         \\\"Conditions: committed financing documented and no reported diligence/financing contingency — Light; no Heavy trigger \\\"\\n         \\\"reported. Consideration: cash. Rollover not a condition.\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"The Buyer Group offered $80.70 per share, in cash, and Bidder 2 offered $80.35 per share, in cash.\\\", 25),\\n            q(\\\"The form of merger agreement and other transaction documentation submitted by the Buyer Group were more favorable to the Company (including because they were less conditional and more likely to be completed and because they offered more certainty of protection for the Company in the unlikely event of non-completion of the transaction) and reflected substantially more acceptance of the Company’s positions.\\\", 25),\\n            q(\\\"On December 6, 2014, the Buyer Group and Bidder 2 submitted their respective comments on the draft merger agreement and other transaction documents, and the Buyer Group provided its financing commitment documents.\\\", 25)],\\n    src=['P-025','P-022'], main='P-025', review='Q4', count=1,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,10), dto=D(2014,12,10), wdate=D(2014,12,10), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=80.70, phigh=80.70, pkind='Point', porigin='Stated', ccy='USD', allcash='Yes', cashclose=80.70,\\n    conddetail='Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: not disclosed; Excl: not stated',\\n    duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=25, related='R020; R043', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R036\\nadd(when='12/10/2014', who='Bidder 2', what='Bid', process=1, round='3', type='Financial',\\n    terms=(\\\"Final bid: $80.35 per share, in cash, submitted with a revised merger agreement and other transaction documents. \\\"\\n           \\\"Not dependent on a Longview rollover; Bidder 2 said it would consider accommodating a rollover only after execution \\\"\\n           \\\"of a merger agreement with the Company.\\\"),\\n    formality='Formal', cond_level='Light',\\n    why=(\\\"Formality: revised merger agreement and transaction documents returned with a solicited final bid (signal 1). \\\"\\n         \\\"Conditions: Light — subject to final documentation; no Heavy trigger reported; financing not stated at this date but \\\"\\n         \\\"commitment documents followed on 12/12 (silence neither raises nor lowers).\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"Bidder 2 offered $80.35 per share, in cash.\\\", 25),\\n            q(\\\"neither the Buyer Group nor Bidder 2 ruled out the possibility of partnering with Longview in a transaction, though Bidder 2 indicated that any partnering with Longview would only occur after completion of bidding and execution of a definitive merger agreement with the Company.\\\", 25)],\\n    src=['P-025'], main='P-025', review='Q4', count=1,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,10), dto=D(2014,12,10), wdate=D(2014,12,10), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=80.35, phigh=80.35, pkind='Point', porigin='Stated', ccy='USD', allcash='Yes', cashclose=80.35,\\n    conddetail='Fin: not stated; DD required: not stated; DD open: not disclosed; Excl: not stated',\\n    duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=25, related='R025; R042', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R037\\nadd(when='12/10/2014', who='Bidder 3', what='Bid', process=1, round='3', type='Financial',\\n    terms=(\\\"Bound: ≤ ~$78 — verbally communicated to J.P. Morgan that Bidder 3's valuation would not be above the current \\\"\\n           \\\"stock price of approximately $78 per share. Ceiling on a valuation level; no share price was submitted, and J.P. \\\"\\n           \\\"Morgan said it was unlikely to be competitive.\\\"),\\n    formality='Informal', cond_level='Insufficient evidence',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated bound on a valuation (one-sided ceiling; Price high = 78 with the filer's 'approximately' noted; no low \\\"\\n         \\\"endpoint). Formality Informal: verbal indication, no documentation. Conditions: nothing stated about financing or \\\"\\n         \\\"diligence for this indication.\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"Bidder 3 verbally communicated to J.P. Morgan that their valuation would not be above the current stock price of approximately $78 per share. J.P. Morgan communicated to Bidder 3 that it was unlikely to be competitive and accordingly Bidder 3 did not submit a written offer.\\\", 25)],\\n    src=['P-025'], main='P-025', review='Q4', count=1,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,10), dto=D(2014,12,10), wdate=D(2014,12,10), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=None, phigh=78.0, pkind='Bound only', porigin='Stated', ccy='USD', allcash='Not stated', cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail='Fin: not stated; DD required: not stated; DD open: not disclosed; Excl: not stated',\\n    duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=25, related='R028; R038', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R038\\nadd(when='12/10/2014', who='Bidder 3', what='Did not submit', process=1, round='3', type='Financial',\\n    terms=(\\\"After communicating a valuation at or below approximately $78 per share and being told that it was unlikely to be \\\"\\n           \\\"competitive, Bidder 3 did not submit a written offer in the final-bid solicitation. Target discouragement followed \\\"\\n           \\\"by non-participation; the bound at R037 is not a submitted share price.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated non-submission (directly reported, not inferred). Decided by Both (target discouragement + bidder \\\"\\n         \\\"non-participation); reason: value at or below market price (stated benchmark ~$78).\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"J.P. Morgan communicated to Bidder 3 that it was unlikely to be competitive and accordingly Bidder 3 did not submit a written offer.\\\", 25)],\\n    src=['P-025'], main='P-025', review='Q5', count=1,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,10), dto=D(2014,12,10), wdate=D(2014,12,10), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby='Both', exitreason='Value at or below market price', obasis='Stated',\\n    page=25, related='R037', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R039\\nadd(when='12/10/2014', who='Ad hoc committee', what='Deadline revised', process=1, round='3', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"Existing due date changed: after reviewing the 12/10 bids, the ad hoc committee — believing neither bid would be \\\"\\n           \\\"approved unless improved and that neither represented the bidders' best offers — instructed J.P. Morgan to tell \\\"\\n           \\\"each bidder to increase its bid and to submit improved bids on 12/12/2014. Old due date 12/10/2014; new due date \\\"\\n           \\\"12/12/2014. On the evening of 12/11 J.P. Morgan also confirmed Longview's continued interest in a rollover.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated revision/extension of the round's final solicitation (not a new round). Requested by the target side; reason \\\"\\n         \\\"stated. New due date in the structured field.\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"the ad hoc committee instructed J.P. Morgan to inform each bidder that it would need to increase its bid, and to instruct the bidders to submit improved bids on December 12, 2014.\\\", 25)],\\n    src=['P-026'], main='P-026', review='Q6', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,10), dto=D(2014,12,10), wdate=D(2014,12,10), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=D(2014,12,12), dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=25, related='R034; R040; R041', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R040\\nadd(when='12/12/2014 (evening)', who='PetSmart / bidders', what='Deadline', process=1, round='3', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"Improved-bid deadline reached. Bidder 2 submitted $81.50 per share in cash and confirmed through J.P. Morgan that \\\"\\n           \\\"it was its best and final offer; the Buyer Group submitted $83.00 per share in cash as its best and final offer \\\"\\n           \\\"(after an interim oral $82.50). Treatment: Enforced — the board took its next step (approval of the Buyer Group on \\\"\\n           \\\"12/13/2014) on the bids in hand.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated milestone; treatment per what followed in the round.\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"During the evening of December 12, 2014, Bidder 2 submitted an offer of $81.50 per share, in cash.\\\", 26)],\\n    src=['P-029'], main='P-029', review='Q6', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,12), dto=D(2014,12,12), wdate=D(2014,12,12), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=D(2014,12,12), dtreat='Enforced', rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=26, related='R039; R042; R043; R044; R045', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R041\\nadd(when='12/12/2014 (approval and confidentiality agreement; 12/09 introductory meetings)',\\n    who='Longview; Buyer Group; ad hoc committee', what='Material process update', process=1, round='3', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"Support: Longview (rollover) — Longview rollover/voting support formed: J.P. Morgan arranged introductory meetings \\\"\\n           \\\"between Longview and the Buyer Group and between Longview and Bidder 2 on 12/09 (attended by J.P. Morgan and \\\"\\n           \\\"Wachtell Lipton; bidders prohibited from disclosing intended bid prices to Longview). Early on 12/12 the Buyer Group \\\"\\n           \\\"requested permission to work more closely with Longview, saying Longview participation might help it achieve a \\\"\\n           \\\"higher price; the ad hoc committee approved, and later that day Longview and the Buyer Group entered a \\\"\\n           \\\"confidentiality agreement permitting exchange of detailed information including bid price. Wachtell Lipton was \\\"\\n           \\\"instructed to provide a voting-agreement form to Longview. The rollover and voting agreements were executed 12/14 \\\"\\n           \\\"(R047). Bidder 2 said a rollover accommodation would not affect its price and would be considered only after a \\\"\\n           \\\"definitive agreement.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated support formation (at most one formation row per instruction §4). Working date = the dated approval day. \\\"\\n         \\\"Longview is a rolling-over shareholder, not a bidding-unit member (no membership change).\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"Early in the day on December 12, 2014, the Buyer Group requested permission to work more closely with Longview in order to include a rollover of a portion of the Company shares managed by Longview in the Buyer Group’s bid. The Buyer Group informed J.P. Morgan that the Buyer Group was working to achieve a higher price, and that Longview participation with the Buyer Group might enhance the Buyer Group’s ability to do so.\\\", 25),\\n            q(\\\"After consultation with the Company’s financial and legal advisors, the ad hoc committee approved the Buyer Group’s request, and, later that day, Longview and the Buyer Group entered into a confidentiality agreement permitting the exchange of detailed information between them, including bid price, which had not previously been shared with Longview.\\\", 25)],\\n    src=['P-027','P-028','P-024','XROLL','XVOTE'], main='P-027', review='Q7', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,12), dto=D(2014,12,12), wdate=D(2014,12,12), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=25, related='R042; R043; R044; R047', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R042\\nadd(when='12/12/2014 (evening)', who='Bidder 2', what='Bid', process=1, round='3', type='Financial',\\n    terms=(\\\"Improved and best-and-final offer: $81.50 per share, in cash; J.P. Morgan confirmed by conversation on 12/12 that \\\"\\n           \\\"$81.50 was Bidder 2's best and final offer. It also submitted a revised draft of the merger agreement and other \\\"\\n           \\\"transaction agreements and financing commitment documents.\\\"),\\n    formality='Formal', cond_level='Light',\\n    why=(\\\"Formality: returned revised transaction documents and financing commitments responding to the best-and-final \\\"\\n         \\\"solicitation (signals 1–2). Conditions: Light — committed financing documented and no Heavy trigger reported.\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"During the evening of December 12, 2014, Bidder 2 submitted an offer of $81.50 per share, in cash. Representatives of J.P. Morgan confirmed via a conversation with Bidder 2 on the evening of December 12, 2014 that $81.50 per share was its best and final offer.\\\", 26),\\n            q(\\\"In addition, each bidder submitted a revised draft of the merger agreement and other transaction agreements, and copies of their respective financing commitment documents.\\\", 26)],\\n    src=['P-029'], main='P-029', review='Q4', count=0,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,12), dto=D(2014,12,12), wdate=D(2014,12,12), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=81.50, phigh=81.50, pkind='Point', porigin='Stated', ccy='USD', allcash='Yes', cashclose=81.50,\\n    conddetail='Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: not disclosed; Excl: not stated',\\n    duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=26, related='R036; R046', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R043\\nadd(when='12/12/2014 (evening)', who='Buyer Group', what='Bid', process=1, round='3', type='Financial',\\n    terms=(\\\"Interim oral offer: $82.50 per share, in cash, with a statement that the Buyer Group was working to increase the \\\"\\n           \\\"offer within the next few hours; superseded later the same evening by the $83.00 best-and-final offer (R044). \\\"\\n           \\\"Preserved as made; not retrospectively upgraded.\\\"),\\n    formality='Formal', cond_level='Light',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated interim oral offer. Formality carried forward from the Buyer Group's formal documentation established in the \\\"\\n         \\\"final-bid stage (continuing proposal); Conditions Light as at R044.\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"The Buyer Group initially submitted an oral offer of $82.50 per share, in cash, but stated that it was working to increase the offer within the next few hours.\\\", 26),\\n            q(\\\"the Buyer Group informed representatives of the Company that after increasing its offer from $82.50 to $83.00 per share, some members of the group, or all of them, were unwilling or unable to offer additional consideration.\\\", 27)],\\n    src=['P-029','XPROC'], main='P-029', review='Q4', count=0,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,12), dto=D(2014,12,12), wdate=D(2014,12,12), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=82.50, phigh=82.50, pkind='Point', porigin='Stated', ccy='USD', allcash='Yes', cashclose=82.50,\\n    conddetail='Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: not disclosed; Excl: not stated',\\n    duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=26, related='R035; R044', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R044\\nadd(when='12/12/2014 (evening)', who='Buyer Group', what='Bid', process=1, round='3', type='Financial',\\n    terms=(\\\"Best-and-final offer: $83.00 per share, in cash; submitted with a revised draft of the merger agreement and other \\\"\\n           \\\"transaction agreements and copies of financing commitment documents. The Buyer Group's versions were, with few \\\"\\n           \\\"exceptions, in substantially executable form; after raising from $82.50 some or all members were unwilling or \\\"\\n           \\\"unable to offer more, and Longview's participation with respect to $250 million of common stock was helpful to \\\"\\n           \\\"achieving $83.00.\\\"),\\n    formality='Formal', cond_level='Light',\\n    why=(\\\"Formality: substantially executable returned agreement and financing commitments responding to the best-and-final \\\"\\n         \\\"solicitation (signals 1–2). Conditions: committed financing, no reported diligence/financing contingency — Light; \\\"\\n         \\\"no Heavy trigger. Consideration all cash for cashed-out shares (rollover explained separately).\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"Later in the evening, the Buyer Group submitted a best and final offer of $83.00 per share, in cash.\\\", 26),\\n            q(\\\"The versions submitted by the Buyer Group were, with few exceptions, in substantially executable form.\\\", 26),\\n            q(\\\"The Buyer Group also informed representatives of the Company that Longview’s willingness to participate in the Buyer Group with respect to $250 million of the common stock was helpful in achieving an $83.00 per share price.\\\", 27)],\\n    src=['P-029','XPROC'], main='P-029', review='Q4', count=0,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,12), dto=D(2014,12,12), wdate=D(2014,12,12), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=83.00, phigh=83.00, pkind='Point', porigin='Stated', ccy='USD', allcash='Yes', cashclose=83.00,\\n    conddetail='Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: not disclosed; Excl: not stated',\\n    duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=26, related='R035; R043; R047', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R045\\nadd(when='12/13/2014', who='PetSmart board', what='Target decision', process=1, round='3', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"Board reviewed the final bids and the proposed transaction; J.P. Morgan rendered its oral fairness opinion \\\"\\n           \\\"(subsequently confirmed in writing) that the $83.00 per share cash consideration was fair from a financial point \\\"\\n           \\\"of view; the board unanimously determined the merger advisable and in the best interests of PetSmart and its \\\"\\n           \\\"stockholders and resolved to recommend approval, subject to confirmation that the remaining open points in the \\\"\\n           \\\"merger agreement had been satisfactorily resolved. The board could reconvene if the ad hoc committee or chairman \\\"\\n           \\\"deemed necessary.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated approval/selection decision; the winning bidder and price identified. Ordinary fairness/approval details folded \\\"\\n         \\\"in because their timing and qualifications are material.\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"Following extensive discussion, the board unanimously determined that the merger agreement and the transactions contemplated thereby, including the merger, were advisable and in the best interests of PetSmart and its stockholders, and to recommend that the Company’s stockholders approve the adoption of the merger agreement. The board’s determination was subject, however, to confirmation that the remaining open points in the merger agreement had been satisfactorily resolved\\\", 26)],\\n    src=['P-030'], main='P-030', review='', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,13), dto=D(2014,12,13), wdate=D(2014,12,13), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=26, related='R044; R046; R047', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R046\\nadd(when='12/14/2014 (Buyer Group selected 12/13/2014; agreement signed 12/14/2014)',\\n    who='Bidder 2', what='Not selected at signing', process=1, round='3', type='Financial',\\n    terms=(\\\"Bidder 2 remained live through its $81.50 best-and-final offer; the target negotiated with two other bidding \\\"\\n           \\\"groups but neither was willing to make a definitive offer above $81.50, and the board chose the Buyer Group's \\\"\\n           \\\"$83.00. Outcome basis Stated (the filing reports the negotiation outcome and Bidder 2's best-and-final price).\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated outcome: still bidding when the target chose another bidder; no earlier withdrawal. Decided by Target; reason: \\\"\\n         \\\"lower offer than the winning bid.\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"ultimately negotiated with the Buyer Group as well as two other bidding groups, neither of which was willing to make a definitive offer at a price above $81.50, which was lower than the $83.00 price offered by the Buyer Group. The board noted that Bidder 2 had informed the Company’s representatives that $81.50 per share was its best and final offer.\\\", 27)],\\n    src=['XPROC','P-031'], main='XPROC', review='Q2', count=1,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,14), dto=D(2014,12,14), wdate=D(2014,12,14), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby='Target', exitreason='Lower offer than rivals', obasis='Stated',\\n    page=27, related='R042; R047', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R047\\nadd(when='12/14/2014', who='PetSmart; Argos Holdings Inc. (Parent); Argos Merger Sub Inc.', what='Merger agreement signed',\\n    process=1, round='3', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"Support: Longview (rollover) — Agreed consideration $83.00 per share in cash for each outstanding share (other than \\\"\\n           \\\"excluded/appraisal shares). Longview contributes 3,012,050 shares (≈$250 million worth) to Parent immediately before \\\"\\n           \\\"the effective time for equity interests and receives $83.00 on its other shares; the voting agreement covers \\\"\\n           \\\"7,424,591 shares. The merger is not subject to a financing condition; committed cash equity up to ~$1.83 billion \\\"\\n           \\\"and committed debt up to $6.95 billion ($4.3bn term loan B, $750m ABL, $1.9bn bridge/notes), with ~$425 million \\\"\\n           \\\"cash on hand and total funds of ~$8.4 billion. Termination fees $255 million (Company) / $510 million (Parent, \\\"\\n           \\\"several Buyer Group termination-fee commitments); end date 06/14/2015. No go-shop; the 15 signers' standstills \\\"\\n           \\\"limit post-signing bids.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated execution of the merger agreement, voting agreement and related transaction agreements (signing is not an extra \\\"\\n         \\\"submitted bid; structured bid-price and formality/conditionality fields intentionally blank). Consideration and \\\"\\n         \\\"support terms stated; per-share price for cash consideration.\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"On December 14, 2014, the parties executed the merger agreement, the voting agreement and related transaction agreements and issued a press release announcing the transaction.\\\", 26),\\n            q(\\\"Under the voting agreement, Longview agreed, among other things, to vote or cause to be voted 7,424,591 shares of common stock, which represent approximately 7.5% of the total outstanding shares of common stock as of the close of business on the record date, in favor of the adoption of the merger agreement\\\", 45),\\n            q(\\\"Longview has agreed to contribute 3,012,050 shares (“rollover shares”) to Parent immediately prior to the effective time in exchange for equity interests in Parent.\\\", 41)],\\n    src=['P-031','XVOTE','XROLL','XFIN','XNOFIN','XCTF','XPTF'], main='P-031', review='', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,14), dto=D(2014,12,14), wdate=D(2014,12,14), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=26, related='R041; R044; R045; R046; R048', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R048\\nadd(when='12/14/2014', who='PetSmart; Parent', what='Merger announced', process=1, round='3', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"Press release issued announcing the transaction, together with execution of the merger agreement, voting agreement \\\"\\n           \\\"and related transaction agreements.\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated publicity; kept separate from signing and closing.\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"and issued a press release announcing the transaction.\\\", 26)],\\n    src=['P-031'], main='P-031', review='', count=None,\\n    dfrom=D(2014,12,14), dto=D(2014,12,14), wdate=D(2014,12,14), basis='Reported day', method='Reported',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=26, related='R047', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# R049\\nadd(when='by 01/29/2015 (record date; retention date not disclosed)', who='Innisfree M&A Incorporated',\\n    what='Adviser engaged', process=1, round='post', type='',\\n    terms=(\\\"Proxy solicitation firm retained to assist with the special-meeting solicitation; approximately $182,725 paid as of \\\"\\n           \\\"the 01/29/2015 record date and approximately $240,000 expected in total through March 2015. Other adviser \\\"\\n           \\\"relationships (engagement date not disclosed).\\\"),\\n    formality='', cond_level='',\\n    why=(\\\"Stated retention and fees. Included as a disclosed adviser; Working date = 01/29/2015 upper bound (assigned; retention \\\"\\n         \\\"date undisclosed).\\\"),\\n    quotes=[q(\\\"Innisfree M&A Incorporated, a proxy solicitation firm, has been retained to assist it in the solicitation of proxies for the special meeting. As of the record date, the Company has paid Innisfree M&A Incorporated approximately $182,725 for the solicitation of proxies in connection with the special meeting and other advisory work, and expects to pay Innisfree M&A Incorporated, in the aggregate, approximately $240,000 through March 2015.\\\", 20)],\\n    src=['XINN'], main='XINN', review='Q7', count=None,\\n    dfrom=None, dto=D(2015,1,29), wdate=D(2015,1,29), basis='Relative only', method='Assigned: bound',\\n    plow=None, phigh=None, pkind=None, porigin=None, ccy=None, allcash=None, cashclose=None,\\n    conddetail=None, duedate=None, dtreat=None, rfinal=None, decidedby=None, exitreason=None, obasis=None,\\n    page=20, related='', deal='petsmart')\\n\\n# Assign # and Row ids\\nfor i, r in enumerate(LA, start=1):\\n    r['num'] = i\\n    r['rid'] = f'R{i:03d}'\\n\\nprint('rows:', len(LA))\\njson.dump(LA, open('/tmp/opencode/petsmart/ledger_draft.json','w'), ensure_ascii=False, default=str, indent=1)\\njson.dump(src_rows, open('/tmp/opencode/petsmart/source_rows.json','w'), ensure_ascii=False, indent=1)\\nprint('done')\\n\", \"path\": \"/tmp/opencode/petsmart/build_data.py\"}"},"time":{"start":1789824941848,"end":1789825021513}}}}
