{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825257645,"sessionID":"ses_f46293c76ffe0Qb4SRXqQEDupS","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e60bbd001r58JyARGPlrTdw","sessionID":"ses_f46293c76ffe0Qb4SRXqQEDupS","messageID":"msg_0b9e5fc35001udyBdKpSn9Z4ly","type":"tool","id":"call_00_oqi4U6Rez8mXGdqpUeJj8703","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode/petsmart && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport openpyxl, textwrap\nwb = openpyxl.load_workbook('/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/petsmart.xlsx')\nws = wb['Deal ledger']\nhdr=[c.value for c in ws[1]]; idx={h:i for i,h in enumerate(hdr)}\ndef show(rid):\n    for row in ws.iter_rows(min_row=2, values_only=True):\n        if row[14]==rid:\n            d={h:row[i] for h,i in idx.items()}\n            print('='*100); print(rid, '|', d['When'], '|', d['What happened'], '| Round', d['Round'])\n            for k in ['Who','Terms or outcome','Formality','Conditions level','Price low','Price high','Price kind','Price origin','All cash','Cash at closing','Conditions detail','Due date','Deadline treatment','Round finality','Decided by','Exit reason','Outcome basis','Count','Date from','Date to','Working date','Date basis','Date method','Page','Related rows']:\n                v=d[k]\n                if v not in (None,''):\n                    print(f'  {k}: {v}')\n            print('  Why:', textwrap.shorten(d['Why and evidence'], 400))\n            print('  Source:', d['Source'], '| Review:', d['Review'])\n            return\nfor rid in ['R016','R017','R018','R024','R026','R028','R029','R034','R038','R041','R047']:\n    show(rid)\nEOF"},"output":"====================================================================================================\nR016 | first week of October 2014 | Round opened | Round 1\n  Who: PetSmart / J.P. Morgan\n  Terms or outcome: R1 anchor: confidentiality-agreement wave (first week of October 2014) — the first target-organized step that admitted participants to a stage; the filing reports no clean target-initiated outreach wave, and parties largely contacted or were contacted by J.P. Morgan / learned of the process from the 08/19 announcement. Rejected candidate anchors: Aug 13 board decision (R010), Aug 19 public announcement (R012), aggregate contacts (R013/R014), Oct 3 board meeting (R015). Round 1 purpose: confidentiality, diligence access and non-binding IOI solicitation. Round finality: Not final — no final/binding or best-and-final designation; the round closed with non-binding indications of interest.\n  Round finality: Not final\n  Date from: 2014-10-01 00:00:00\n  Date to: 2014-10-07 00:00:00\n  Working date: 2014-10-04 00:00:00\n  Date basis: Reported interval\n  Date method: Assigned: midpoint\n  Page: 23\n  Related rows: R010; R012; R013; R014; R015; R017\n  Why: Convention (round map): round opens under the instruction's rule 3 (no target outreach wave; first target-organized admitting step) anchored on the confidentiality wave; Working date = calendar midpoint of the first-week window (assigned). Quotation: “In the first week of October 2014, the Company entered into confidentiality and standstill agreements with 15 potentially interested financial [...]\n  Source: P-013 | Review: Q1\n====================================================================================================\nR017 | first week of October 2014 (signings); diligence during October 2014 | NDA signed | Round 1\n  Who: 15 financial buyers (cohort)\n  Terms or outcome: Company entered confidentiality and standstill agreements with 15 potentially interested financial buyers; all 15 then engaged in due diligence during October, received management presentations involving senior-most management, and received detailed financial and business-plan information including the Profit Improvement Plan. The standstills prevent the 15 from submitting (or even seeking permission to submit) a higher bid once a definitive agreement is signed; the board believed this promoted best bids. New signatures in this process; no reused coverage from an earlier attempt. Uniform stage access — any access differences are recorded at R030.\n  Count: 15\n  Date from: 2014-10-01 00:00:00\n  Date to: 2014-10-07 00:00:00\n  Working date: 2014-10-04 00:00:00\n  Date basis: Reported interval\n  Date method: Assigned: midpoint\n  Page: 23\n  Related rows: R016; R024; R020\n  Why: Stated: 15 signers, all financial buyers. Count 15 = cohort size at this step. Scope: signers did not all become bidders (see R024). Quotations: “In the first week of October 2014, the Company entered into confidentiality and standstill agreements with 15 potentially interested financial buyers, all 15 of which, during the month of October engaged in due diligence, received management [...]\n  Source: P-013; X-021 | Review: Q2; Q5\n====================================================================================================\nR018 | October 2014 (communication date not disclosed) | Deadline set | Round 1\n  Who: PetSmart / J.P. Morgan (to the 15 potential bidders)\n  Terms or outcome: Potential bidders were informed that non-binding preliminary indications of interest would be due October 30, 2014. They were also told that Longview was willing to 'roll-over' up to 7.5 million shares on terms and price acceptable to Longview (such shares would not receive cash consideration and could remain equity) and were asked to indicate interest in Longview participation, which was not a condition to participation. Communication date within October not disclosed; known only to precede 10/30/2014.\n  Due date: 2014-10-30 00:00:00\n  Date from: 2014-10-01 00:00:00\n  Date to: 2014-10-29 00:00:00\n  Working date: 2014-10-15 00:00:00\n  Date basis: Reported interval\n  Date method: Assigned: midpoint\n  Page: 23\n  Related rows: R019; R041\n  Why: Stated deadline communication plus stage information on the rollover. Working date = midpoint of the October window before the due date (assigned; order must follow the NDA row). Quotations: “During October, the potential bidders were informed that non-binding preliminary indications of interest would be due on October 30, 2014.” (p. 23) “The potential bidders were also informed that [...]\n  Source: P-014; P-015 | Review: Q6; Q8\n====================================================================================================\nR024 | by 10/30/2014 | Did not submit | Round 1\n  Who: 9 non-submitting NDA signers (cohort)\n  Terms or outcome: Inferred: residual — 15 NDA signers − 6 submitters = 9 non-submitters. The 15 potential bidders were told IOIs were due 10/30/2014; six submitted indications and no submission is reported for the other nine. Row records only non-submission at this solicitation, not permanent withdrawal.\n  Decided by: Unknown\n  Exit reason: Not stated\n  Outcome basis: Inferred: residual\n  Count: 9\n  Date to: 2014-10-30 00:00:00\n  Working date: 2014-10-30 00:00:00\n  Date basis: Relative only\n  Date method: Assigned: deadline\n  Page: 24\n  Related rows: R017; R020; R021; R022; R023\n  Why: Inferred: residual (base assumes all 15 confidentiality signers were invited to submit and that the six stated submitters exhaust the submissions). Arithmetic in Terms. No identities, motives or decision dates inferred. Quotations: “the potential bidders were informed that non-binding preliminary indications of interest would be due on October 30, 2014.” (p. 23) “On October 30, six of the [...]\n  Source: P-014; P-016; P-013 | Review: Q5\n====================================================================================================\nR026 | 11/03/2014 | Round opened | Round 2\n  Who: PetSmart board\n  Terms or outcome: R2 opens: board met and allowed the four bidders that had indicated a price or range at or above $80.00 per share to proceed to the 'final round of the sale process'. Individually described ≥$80 units: Buyer Group (R020), Bidder 2 (R025, raised from $78) and unnamed bidder 1 (R022); one further ≥$80 submitter sits inside residual R023. Purpose: finalist diligence and negotiation toward definitive documentation. Round finality: Inferred final — selected bidders moved toward a definitive agreement; the filing calls it the board's final round, but no announcement to bidders of a binding/best-and-final stage is quoted at this opening.\n  Round finality: Inferred final\n  Date from: 2014-11-03 00:00:00\n  Date to: 2014-11-03 00:00:00\n  Working date: 2014-11-03 00:00:00\n  Date basis: Reported day\n  Date method: Reported\n  Page: 24\n  Related rows: R020; R022; R023; R025; R027; R028; R029\n  Why: Stated selection threshold and count; round map per instruction. See Q1/Q2 on the four-bidder composition. Quotation: “On November 3, 2014, the board met in person, together with members of management and representatives of J.P. Morgan and Wachtell Lipton, to continue its review of strategic alternatives, including a review of the indications of interest. The board determined to allow the [...]\n  Source: P-017 | Review: Q1; Q2\n====================================================================================================\nR028 | after 11/03/2014; day not disclosed | Bidding group changed | Round 2\n  Who: Bidder 3 (two unnamed final-round bidders working together)\n  Terms or outcome: Two bidders — one invited into the final round that indicated a desire to work with an equity partner given the size of a PetSmart acquisition, and one that had indicated it would drop out of the process if not permitted to work together with another bidder — requested permission to work together (they had worked together successfully in prior large leveraged buyouts); the ad hoc committee authorized them, and the two are referred to together as 'Bidder 3'. Effect on final-round units: 4 admitted bidders → 3 bidding units (units −1). Because the members are not independently tracked elsewhere, this row states the unit effect rather than opening per-member Joined group rows; unit arithmetic keeps the stage balance intact.\n  Count: 2\n  Date from: 2014-11-04 00:00:00\n  Working date: 2014-11-04 00:00:00\n  Date basis: Relative only\n  Date method: Assigned: bound\n  Page: 24\n  Related rows: R026; R037; R038\n  Why: Stated formation and authorization. Convention: anonymous-pair treatment of the unit change (instruction §5.3); identity of members vs Unnamed bidder 1 (R022) not established (Q2). Quotation: “Two of the bidders (one of which had been invited into the final round but had indicated a desire to work with an equity partner in light of the size of an acquisition of PetSmart, and the other of [...]\n  Source: P-018 | Review: Q2\n====================================================================================================\nR029 | November 2014 (day not disclosed) | Round opened | Round 3\n  Who: PetSmart\n  Terms or outcome: R3 anchor: first request for final bids — the Company circulated a form of merger agreement to the bidders with instructions that bidders submit any proposed comments on the merger agreement together with their final bids; bidders also engaged in further extensive due diligence and management presentations during November. Rejected candidate anchors: the 12/04–12/05 setting of the 12/10 final-bid deadline (R033/R034) — treated as deadline history inside R3, not a fresh round; the 11/03 selection (R026) opens R2. Round finality: Announced as final — bidders were instructed to deliver 'final bids' and the Company later set a 'final bids' deadline and confirmed a 'best and final' offer with Bidder 2.\n  Round finality: Announced as final\n  Date from: 2014-11-01 00:00:00\n  Date to: 2014-11-30 00:00:00\n  Working date: 2014-11-15 00:00:00\n  Date basis: Reported interval\n  Date method: Assigned: midpoint\n  Page: 24\n  Related rows: R026; R033\n  Why: Round-map convention: the instruction makes the first request for final offers a new round even with unchanged bidders; the November circulation is that request. Working date = November midpoint (assigned; day not disclosed). Quotations: “Also during November, the Company circulated a form of merger agreement to the bidders with instructions that the bidders submit any proposed comments on [...]\n  Source: P-019 | Review: Q1\n====================================================================================================\nR034 | 12/10/2014 (evening) | Deadline | Round 3\n  Who: PetSmart / bidders\n  Terms or outcome: Final-bid deadline reached. PetSmart received final bid letters with revised merger agreement and transaction documents from the Buyer Group and Bidder 2, plus a verbal indication from Bidder 3. Treatment: Extended — after reviewing the bids on 12/10 the ad hoc committee asked the same bidders to submit improved bids on 12/12/2014 (Deadline revised, R039).\n  Due date: 2014-12-10 00:00:00\n  Deadline treatment: Extended\n  Date from: 2014-12-10 00:00:00\n  Date to: 2014-12-10 00:00:00\n  Working date: 2014-12-10 00:00:00\n  Date basis: Reported day\n  Date method: Reported\n  Page: 25\n  Related rows: R033; R035; R036; R037; R039\n  Why: Stated due-date milestone; treatment Extended because the Deadline revised row R039 moves this due date. Quotation: “On December 10, PetSmart received final bid letters along with revised versions of the merger agreement and other transaction documents from the Buyer Group and from Bidder 2 and a verbal indication from Bidder 3.” (p. 25)\n  Source: P-025; P-026 | Review: Q6\n====================================================================================================\nR038 | 12/10/2014 | Did not submit | Round 3\n  Who: Bidder 3\n  Terms or outcome: After communicating a valuation at or below approximately $78 per share and being told that it was unlikely to be competitive, Bidder 3 did not submit a written offer in the final-bid solicitation. Target discouragement followed by non-participation; the bound at R037 is not a submitted share price.\n  Decided by: Both\n  Exit reason: Value at or below market price\n  Outcome basis: Stated\n  Count: 1\n  Date from: 2014-12-10 00:00:00\n  Date to: 2014-12-10 00:00:00\n  Working date: 2014-12-10 00:00:00\n  Date basis: Reported day\n  Date method: Reported\n  Page: 25\n  Related rows: R037\n  Why: Stated non-submission (directly reported, not inferred). Decided by Both (target discouragement + bidder non-participation); reason: value at or below market price (stated benchmark ~$78). Quotation: “J.P. Morgan communicated to Bidder 3 that it was unlikely to be competitive and accordingly Bidder 3 did not submit a written offer.” (p. 25)\n  Source: P-025 | Review: Q5\n====================================================================================================\nR041 | 12/12/2014 (approval and confidentiality agreement; 12/09 introductory meetings) | Material process update | Round 3\n  Who: Longview; Buyer Group; ad hoc committee\n  Terms or outcome: Support: Longview (rollover) — Longview rollover/voting support formed: J.P. Morgan arranged introductory meetings between Longview and the Buyer Group and between Longview and Bidder 2 on 12/09 (attended by J.P. Morgan and Wachtell Lipton; bidders prohibited from disclosing intended bid prices to Longview). Early on 12/12 the Buyer Group requested permission to work more closely with Longview, saying Longview participation might help it achieve a higher price; the ad hoc committee approved, and later that day Longview and the Buyer Group entered a confidentiality agreement permitting exchange of detailed information including bid price. Wachtell Lipton was instructed to provide a voting-agreement form to Longview. The rollover and voting agreements were executed 12/14 (R047). Bidder 2 said a rollover accommodation would not affect its price and would be considered only after a definitive agreement.\n  Date from: 2014-12-12 00:00:00\n  Date to: 2014-12-12 00:00:00\n  Working date: 2014-12-12 00:00:00\n  Date basis: Reported day\n  Date method: Reported\n  Page: 25\n  Related rows: R042; R043; R044; R047\n  Why: Stated support formation (at most one formation row per instruction §4). Working date = the dated approval day. Longview is a rolling-over shareholder, not a bidding-unit member (no membership change). Quotations: “Early in the day on December 12, 2014, the Buyer Group requested permission to work more closely with Longview in order to include a rollover of a portion of the Company shares [...]\n  Source: P-027; P-028; P-024; X-033; X-037 | Review: Q7\n====================================================================================================\nR047 | 12/14/2014 | Merger agreement signed | Round 3\n  Who: PetSmart; Argos Holdings Inc. (Parent); Argos Merger Sub Inc.\n  Terms or outcome: Support: Longview (rollover) — Agreed consideration $83.00 per share in cash for each outstanding share (other than excluded/appraisal shares). Longview contributes 3,012,050 shares (≈$250 million worth) to Parent immediately before the effective time for equity interests and receives $83.00 on its other shares; the voting agreement covers 7,424,591 shares. The merger is not subject to a financing condition; committed cash equity up to ~$1.83 billion and committed debt up to $6.95 billion ($4.3bn term loan B, $750m ABL, $1.9bn bridge/notes), with ~$425 million cash on hand and total funds of ~$8.4 billion. Termination fees $255 million (Company) / $510 million (Parent, several Buyer Group termination-fee commitments); end date 06/14/2015. No go-shop; the 15 signers' standstills limit post-signing bids.\n  Date from: 2014-12-14 00:00:00\n  Date to: 2014-12-14 00:00:00\n  Working date: 2014-12-14 00:00:00\n  Date basis: Reported day\n  Date method: Reported\n  Page: 26\n  Related rows: R041; R044; R045; R046; R048\n  Why: Stated execution of the merger agreement, voting agreement and related transaction agreements (signing is not an extra submitted bid; structured bid-price and formality/conditionality fields intentionally blank). Consideration and support terms stated; per-share price for cash consideration. Quotations: “On December 14, 2014, the parties executed the merger agreement, the voting agreement [...]\n  Source: P-031; X-037; X-033; X-007; X-008; X-013; X-014 | Review: None\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"====================================================================================================\nR016 | first week of October 2014 | Round opened | Round 1\n  Who: PetSmart / J.P. Morgan\n  Terms or outcome: R1 anchor: confidentiality-agreement wave (first week of October 2014) — the first target-organized step that admitted participants to a stage; the filing reports no clean target-initiated outreach wave, and parties largely contacted or were contacted by J.P. Morgan / learned of the process from the 08/19 announcement. Rejected candidate anchors: Aug 13 board decision (R010), Aug 19 public announcement (R012), aggregate contacts (R013/R014), Oct 3 board meeting (R015). Round 1 purpose: confidentiality, diligence access and non-binding IOI solicitation. Round finality: Not final — no final/binding or best-and-final designation; the round closed with non-binding indications of interest.\n  Round finality: Not final\n  Date from: 2014-10-01 00:00:00\n  Date to: 2014-10-07 00:00:00\n  Working date: 2014-10-04 00:00:00\n  Date basis: Reported interval\n  Date method: Assigned: midpoint\n  Page: 23\n  Related rows: R010; R012; R013; R014; R015; R017\n  Why: Convention (round map): round opens under the instruction's rule 3 (no target outreach wave; first target-organized admitting step) anchored on the confidentiality wave; Working date = calendar midpoint of the first-week window (assigned). Quotation: “In the first week of October 2014, the Company entered into confidentiality and standstill agreements with 15 potentially interested financial [...]\n  Source: P-013 | Review: Q1\n====================================================================================================\nR017 | first week of October 2014 (signings); diligence during October 2014 | NDA signed | Round 1\n  Who: 15 financial buyers (cohort)\n  Terms or outcome: Company entered confidentiality and standstill agreements with 15 potentially interested financial buyers; all 15 then engaged in due diligence during October, received management presentations involving senior-most management, and received detailed financial and business-plan information including the Profit Improvement Plan. The standstills prevent the 15 from submitting (or even seeking permission to submit) a higher bid once a definitive agreement is signed; the board believed this promoted best bids. New signatures in this process; no reused coverage from an earlier attempt. Uniform stage access — any access differences are recorded at R030.\n  Count: 15\n  Date from: 2014-10-01 00:00:00\n  Date to: 2014-10-07 00:00:00\n  Working date: 2014-10-04 00:00:00\n  Date basis: Reported interval\n  Date method: Assigned: midpoint\n  Page: 23\n  Related rows: R016; R024; R020\n  Why: Stated: 15 signers, all financial buyers. Count 15 = cohort size at this step. Scope: signers did not all become bidders (see R024). Quotations: “In the first week of October 2014, the Company entered into confidentiality and standstill agreements with 15 potentially interested financial buyers, all 15 of which, during the month of October engaged in due diligence, received management [...]\n  Source: P-013; X-021 | Review: Q2; Q5\n====================================================================================================\nR018 | October 2014 (communication date not disclosed) | Deadline set | Round 1\n  Who: PetSmart / J.P. Morgan (to the 15 potential bidders)\n  Terms or outcome: Potential bidders were informed that non-binding preliminary indications of interest would be due October 30, 2014. They were also told that Longview was willing to 'roll-over' up to 7.5 million shares on terms and price acceptable to Longview (such shares would not receive cash consideration and could remain equity) and were asked to indicate interest in Longview participation, which was not a condition to participation. Communication date within October not disclosed; known only to precede 10/30/2014.\n  Due date: 2014-10-30 00:00:00\n  Date from: 2014-10-01 00:00:00\n  Date to: 2014-10-29 00:00:00\n  Working date: 2014-10-15 00:00:00\n  Date basis: Reported interval\n  Date method: Assigned: midpoint\n  Page: 23\n  Related rows: R019; R041\n  Why: Stated deadline communication plus stage information on the rollover. Working date = midpoint of the October window before the due date (assigned; order must follow the NDA row). Quotations: “During October, the potential bidders were informed that non-binding preliminary indications of interest would be due on October 30, 2014.” (p. 23) “The potential bidders were also informed that [...]\n  Source: P-014; P-015 | Review: Q6; Q8\n====================================================================================================\nR024 | by 10/30/2014 | Did not submit | Round 1\n  Who: 9 non-submitting NDA signers (cohort)\n  Terms or outcome: Inferred: residual — 15 NDA signers − 6 submitters = 9 non-submitters. The 15 potential bidders were told IOIs were due 10/30/2014; six submitted indications and no submission is reported for the other nine. Row records only non-submission at this solicitation, not permanent withdrawal.\n  Decided by: Unknown\n  Exit reason: Not stated\n  Outcome basis: Inferred: residual\n  Count: 9\n  Date to: 2014-10-30 00:00:00\n  Working date: 2014-10-30 00:00:00\n  Date basis: Relative only\n  Date method: Assigned: deadline\n  Page: 24\n  Related rows: R017; R020; R021; R022; R023\n  Why: Inferred: residual (base assumes all 15 confidentiality signers were invited to submit and that the six stated submitters exhaust the submissions). Arithmetic in Terms. No identities, motives or decision dates inferred. Quotations: “the potential bidders were informed that non-binding preliminary indications of interest would be due on October 30, 2014.” (p. 23) “On October 30, six of the [...]\n  Source: P-014; P-016; P-013 | Review: Q5\n====================================================================================================\nR026 | 11/03/2014 | Round opened | Round 2\n  Who: PetSmart board\n  Terms or outcome: R2 opens: board met and allowed the four bidders that had indicated a price or range at or above $80.00 per share to proceed to the 'final round of the sale process'. Individually described ≥$80 units: Buyer Group (R020), Bidder 2 (R025, raised from $78) and unnamed bidder 1 (R022); one further ≥$80 submitter sits inside residual R023. Purpose: finalist diligence and negotiation toward definitive documentation. Round finality: Inferred final — selected bidders moved toward a definitive agreement; the filing calls it the board's final round, but no announcement to bidders of a binding/best-and-final stage is quoted at this opening.\n  Round finality: Inferred final\n  Date from: 2014-11-03 00:00:00\n  Date to: 2014-11-03 00:00:00\n  Working date: 2014-11-03 00:00:00\n  Date basis: Reported day\n  Date method: Reported\n  Page: 24\n  Related rows: R020; R022; R023; R025; R027; R028; R029\n  Why: Stated selection threshold and count; round map per instruction. See Q1/Q2 on the four-bidder composition. Quotation: “On November 3, 2014, the board met in person, together with members of management and representatives of J.P. Morgan and Wachtell Lipton, to continue its review of strategic alternatives, including a review of the indications of interest. The board determined to allow the [...]\n  Source: P-017 | Review: Q1; Q2\n====================================================================================================\nR028 | after 11/03/2014; day not disclosed | Bidding group changed | Round 2\n  Who: Bidder 3 (two unnamed final-round bidders working together)\n  Terms or outcome: Two bidders — one invited into the final round that indicated a desire to work with an equity partner given the size of a PetSmart acquisition, and one that had indicated it would drop out of the process if not permitted to work together with another bidder — requested permission to work together (they had worked together successfully in prior large leveraged buyouts); the ad hoc committee authorized them, and the two are referred to together as 'Bidder 3'. Effect on final-round units: 4 admitted bidders → 3 bidding units (units −1). Because the members are not independently tracked elsewhere, this row states the unit effect rather than opening per-member Joined group rows; unit arithmetic keeps the stage balance intact.\n  Count: 2\n  Date from: 2014-11-04 00:00:00\n  Working date: 2014-11-04 00:00:00\n  Date basis: Relative only\n  Date method: Assigned: bound\n  Page: 24\n  Related rows: R026; R037; R038\n  Why: Stated formation and authorization. Convention: anonymous-pair treatment of the unit change (instruction §5.3); identity of members vs Unnamed bidder 1 (R022) not established (Q2). Quotation: “Two of the bidders (one of which had been invited into the final round but had indicated a desire to work with an equity partner in light of the size of an acquisition of PetSmart, and the other of [...]\n  Source: P-018 | Review: Q2\n====================================================================================================\nR029 | November 2014 (day not disclosed) | Round opened | Round 3\n  Who: PetSmart\n  Terms or outcome: R3 anchor: first request for final bids — the Company circulated a form of merger agreement to the bidders with instructions that bidders submit any proposed comments on the merger agreement together with their final bids; bidders also engaged in further extensive due diligence and management presentations during November. Rejected candidate anchors: the 12/04–12/05 setting of the 12/10 final-bid deadline (R033/R034) — treated as deadline history inside R3, not a fresh round; the 11/03 selection (R026) opens R2. Round finality: Announced as final — bidders were instructed to deliver 'final bids' and the Company later set a 'final bids' deadline and confirmed a 'best and final' offer with Bidder 2.\n  Round finality: Announced as final\n  Date from: 2014-11-01 00:00:00\n  Date to: 2014-11-30 00:00:00\n  Working date: 2014-11-15 00:00:00\n  Date basis: Reported interval\n  Date method: Assigned: midpoint\n  Page: 24\n  Related rows: R026; R033\n  Why: Round-map convention: the instruction makes the first request for final offers a new round even with unchanged bidders; the November circulation is that request. Working date = November midpoint (assigned; day not disclosed). Quotations: “Also during November, the Company circulated a form of merger agreement to the bidders with instructions that the bidders submit any proposed comments on [...]\n  Source: P-019 | Review: Q1\n====================================================================================================\nR034 | 12/10/2014 (evening) | Deadline | Round 3\n  Who: PetSmart / bidders\n  Terms or outcome: Final-bid deadline reached. PetSmart received final bid letters with revised merger agreement and transaction documents from the Buyer Group and Bidder 2, plus a verbal indication from Bidder 3. Treatment: Extended — after reviewing the bids on 12/10 the ad hoc committee asked the same bidders to submit improved bids on 12/12/2014 (Deadline revised, R039).\n  Due date: 2014-12-10 00:00:00\n  Deadline treatment: Extended\n  Date from: 2014-12-10 00:00:00\n  Date to: 2014-12-10 00:00:00\n  Working date: 2014-12-10 00:00:00\n  Date basis: Reported day\n  Date method: Reported\n  Page: 25\n  Related rows: R033; R035; R036; R037; R039\n  Why: Stated due-date milestone; treatment Extended because the Deadline revised row R039 moves this due date. Quotation: “On December 10, PetSmart received final bid letters along with revised versions of the merger agreement and other transaction documents from the Buyer Group and from Bidder 2 and a verbal indication from Bidder 3.” (p. 25)\n  Source: P-025; P-026 | Review: Q6\n====================================================================================================\nR038 | 12/10/2014 | Did not submit | Round 3\n  Who: Bidder 3\n  Terms or outcome: After communicating a valuation at or below approximately $78 per share and being told that it was unlikely to be competitive, Bidder 3 did not submit a written offer in the final-bid solicitation. Target discouragement followed by non-participation; the bound at R037 is not a submitted share price.\n  Decided by: Both\n  Exit reason: Value at or below market price\n  Outcome basis: Stated\n  Count: 1\n  Date from: 2014-12-10 00:00:00\n  Date to: 2014-12-10 00:00:00\n  Working date: 2014-12-10 00:00:00\n  Date basis: Reported day\n  Date method: Reported\n  Page: 25\n  Related rows: R037\n  Why: Stated non-submission (directly reported, not inferred). Decided by Both (target discouragement + bidder non-participation); reason: value at or below market price (stated benchmark ~$78). Quotation: “J.P. Morgan communicated to Bidder 3 that it was unlikely to be competitive and accordingly Bidder 3 did not submit a written offer.” (p. 25)\n  Source: P-025 | Review: Q5\n====================================================================================================\nR041 | 12/12/2014 (approval and confidentiality agreement; 12/09 introductory meetings) | Material process update | Round 3\n  Who: Longview; Buyer Group; ad hoc committee\n  Terms or outcome: Support: Longview (rollover) — Longview rollover/voting support formed: J.P. Morgan arranged introductory meetings between Longview and the Buyer Group and between Longview and Bidder 2 on 12/09 (attended by J.P. Morgan and Wachtell Lipton; bidders prohibited from disclosing intended bid prices to Longview). Early on 12/12 the Buyer Group requested permission to work more closely with Longview, saying Longview participation might help it achieve a higher price; the ad hoc committee approved, and later that day Longview and the Buyer Group entered a confidentiality agreement permitting exchange of detailed information including bid price. Wachtell Lipton was instructed to provide a voting-agreement form to Longview. The rollover and voting agreements were executed 12/14 (R047). Bidder 2 said a rollover accommodation would not affect its price and would be considered only after a definitive agreement.\n  Date from: 2014-12-12 00:00:00\n  Date to: 2014-12-12 00:00:00\n  Working date: 2014-12-12 00:00:00\n  Date basis: Reported day\n  Date method: Reported\n  Page: 25\n  Related rows: R042; R043; R044; R047\n  Why: Stated support formation (at most one formation row per instruction §4). Working date = the dated approval day. Longview is a rolling-over shareholder, not a bidding-unit member (no membership change). Quotations: “Early in the day on December 12, 2014, the Buyer Group requested permission to work more closely with Longview in order to include a rollover of a portion of the Company shares [...]\n  Source: P-027; P-028; P-024; X-033; X-037 | Review: Q7\n====================================================================================================\nR047 | 12/14/2014 | Merger agreement signed | Round 3\n  Who: PetSmart; Argos Holdings Inc. (Parent); Argos Merger Sub Inc.\n  Terms or outcome: Support: Longview (rollover) — Agreed consideration $83.00 per share in cash for each outstanding share (other than excluded/appraisal shares). Longview contributes 3,012,050 shares (≈$250 million worth) to Parent immediately before the effective time for equity interests and receives $83.00 on its other shares; the voting agreement covers 7,424,591 shares. The merger is not subject to a financing condition; committed cash equity up to ~$1.83 billion and committed debt up to $6.95 billion ($4.3bn term loan B, $750m ABL, $1.9bn bridge/notes), with ~$425 million cash on hand and total funds of ~$8.4 billion. Termination fees $255 million (Company) / $510 million (Parent, several Buyer Group termination-fee commitments); end date 06/14/2015. No go-shop; the 15 signers' standstills limit post-signing bids.\n  Date from: 2014-12-14 00:00:00\n  Date to: 2014-12-14 00:00:00\n  Working date: 2014-12-14 00:00:00\n  Date basis: Reported day\n  Date method: Reported\n  Page: 26\n  Related rows: R041; R044; R045; R046; R048\n  Why: Stated execution of the merger agreement, voting agreement and related transaction agreements (signing is not an extra submitted bid; structured bid-price and formality/conditionality fields intentionally blank). Consideration and support terms stated; per-share price for cash consideration. Quotations: “On December 14, 2014, the parties executed the merger agreement, the voting agreement [...]\n  Source: P-031; X-037; X-033; X-007; X-008; X-013; X-014 | Review: None\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Command exited with code 0."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /tmp/opencode/petsmart && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nimport openpyxl, textwrap\\nwb = openpyxl.load_workbook('/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/petsmart.xlsx')\\nws = wb['Deal ledger']\\nhdr=[c.value for c in ws[1]]; idx={h:i for i,h in enumerate(hdr)}\\ndef show(rid):\\n    for row in ws.iter_rows(min_row=2, values_only=True):\\n        if row[14]==rid:\\n            d={h:row[i] for h,i in idx.items()}\\n            print('='*100); print(rid, '|', d['When'], '|', d['What happened'], '| Round', d['Round'])\\n            for k in ['Who','Terms or outcome','Formality','Conditions level','Price low','Price high','Price kind','Price origin','All cash','Cash at closing','Conditions detail','Due date','Deadline treatment','Round finality','Decided by','Exit reason','Outcome basis','Count','Date from','Date to','Working date','Date basis','Date method','Page','Related rows']:\\n                v=d[k]\\n                if v not in (None,''):\\n                    print(f'  {k}: {v}')\\n            print('  Why:', textwrap.shorten(d['Why and evidence'], 400))\\n            print('  Source:', d['Source'], '| Review:', d['Review'])\\n            return\\nfor rid in ['R016','R017','R018','R024','R026','R028','R029','R034','R038','R041','R047']:\\n    show(rid)\\nEOF\"}"},"time":{"start":1789825256381,"end":1789825257645}}}}
