{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825266833,"sessionID":"ses_f46293c76ffe0Qb4SRXqQEDupS","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e631cf001guneiOC9Kog0iV","sessionID":"ses_f46293c76ffe0Qb4SRXqQEDupS","messageID":"msg_0b9e610c20019qrrohuBTLvL9k","type":"tool","id":"call_00_ruxnXKAqnJnuzDPa3KlT0973","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode/petsmart && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport openpyxl, textwrap\nwb = openpyxl.load_workbook('/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/petsmart.xlsx')\nqs = wb['Questions']\nfor row in qs.iter_rows(min_row=2, values_only=True):\n    print('='*100)\n    print(row[0], '|', row[1])\n    print('RECOMMENDED:', textwrap.shorten(row[2], 500))\n    print('WHY:', textwrap.shorten(row[3], 350))\n    print('AFFECTED:', row[4])\n    print('CONSEQUENCE:', textwrap.shorten(row[5], 300))\n    print('STATUS:', row[6])\nEOF"},"output":"====================================================================================================\nQ1 | Process and round map: single process; R1 anchor; R2/R3 split; finality values\nRECOMMENDED: Keep one process (the 2014 sale attempt ending in the 12/14/2014 signing). Round 1 opens with the confidentiality-agreement wave (R016 anchor; rejected candidates R010, R012, R013/R014, R015 remain separate rows). Split Round 2 (11/03/2014 selection; Inferred final) from Round 3 (November first request for final bids; Announced as final). Alternatives: a two-round map folding R2/R3, or anchoring R3 on the 12/04–05 final-bid deadline.\nWHY: R1 anchor: the filing reports no clean target outreach wave and parties contacted or were contacted by J.P. Morgan (P-013; P-011). R2/R3: selection to the \"final round\" (P-017) is followed by the merger-agreement circulation with instructions to submit \"final bids\" (P-019) — the instruction makes the first final-offer request a new round. R2 [...]\nAFFECTED: Rounds on R010–R016, R026, R029–R034, R040; Round finality on R016 (Not final), R026 (Inferred final), R029 (Announced as final)\nCONSEQUENCE: Moving the R1 boundary to 08/13, 08/19 or 10/03 shifts R013–R015 into Round 1; folding R2/R3 changes round-bidder tallies (currently R1 = 6, R3 = 3 new units) and the finality labels. Boundary-candidate rows are isolated so either move is mechanical.\nSTATUS: Pending\n====================================================================================================\nQ2 | Round-1 and final-round counts and identities: six IOIs vs \"5 bidder groups\"; four bidders ≥ $80 vs three described ranges; residual cohort; Bidder 3 membership\nRECOMMENDED: Read the six IOI submitters as: Buyer Group ($81–83), Bidder 2 ($78, revised $81–84), Unnamed bidder 1 ($80–85) and a 3-unit residual cohort (one at/above $80, two below). Read the four ≥$80 finalists as Buyer Group, Bidder 2 and the two bidders later forming Bidder 3, so the final round falls to 3 units post-combination. Do not map Unnamed bidder 1 or any specific bidder to a Bidder 3 member.\nWHY: Six submitters stated (P-016); four advanced (P-017); \"5 bidder groups\" (X-020); two bidders formed Bidder 3 (P-018). The filing does not name the members or the fourth ≥$80 unit. The recommended reading makes all counts reconcile without inventing identities.\nAFFECTED: R020–R023 (bids/residual), R026 (four admitted), R027 (two dropped), R028 (Bidder 3 formation), R046 (Bidder 2 outcome)\nCONSEQUENCE: If the two Bidder 3 members were not both among the four admitted, the final round would carry an extra unnamed bidder needing its own close-out and the R2 unit balance would change (currently 4 → 3). If \"5 bidder groups\" counts something else, Round 1 bid units stay 6 but the group tally [...]\nSTATUS: Pending\n====================================================================================================\nQ3 | Bidder types and anonymous identities\nRECOMMENDED: Keep every bidder unit classified Financial on the filing's own description of the 15 signers as \"financial buyers\" (P-013), including Bidder 2, Unnamed bidder 1 and Bidder 3. Do not identify anonymous participants from outside knowledge; no person/entity mapping is asserted for Unnamed bidder 1 or the Bidder 3 members.\nWHY: P-013 describes the confidentiality signers as financial buyers; bidders drew from that population; Bidder 3's members had prior large-LBO experience (P-018). No strategic bidder entered; the winner is a PE-led consortium (X-001).\nAFFECTED: Type cells on R020–R023, R025, R028, R035–R038, R042–R044\nCONSEQUENCE: A different type basis would change cohort descriptions but no counts; leaving the winner Unknown is not supported (BC Partners consortium).\nSTATUS: Pending\n====================================================================================================\nQ4 | Formality and Conditions borderline calls (IOIs; December bids; Bidder 3 bound-only valuation)\nRECOMMENDED: Keep IOIs Informal with Conditions \"Insufficient evidence\" (prices stated, financing/conditions silent, substantive October diligence access context). Keep the 12/10–12/12 Buyer Group and Bidder 2 bids Formal/Light (returned revised transaction documents and financing commitments; no reported Heavy trigger). Keep Bidder 3's verbal ≤ ~$78 indication Informal (no documentation) and its price as Bound only (Price high 78; no low endpoint).\nWHY: IOIs: \"non-binding preliminary indications\" (P-014, P-016). December: final bid letters with \"revised versions of the merger agreement\" (P-025) and, on 12/12, \"revised draft ... and copies of their respective financing commitment documents\", Buyer Group versions \"substantially executable\" (P-029); committed financing per X-023 and X-032. [...]\nAFFECTED: Formality/Conditions on R020–R023, R025, R035–R037, R042–R044; Conditions detail strings on the same rows\nCONSEQUENCE: Reclassifying formality/conditions affects review flags and which signals are credited, not counts. If the IOIs were judged Heavy by context, the conditions labels on R020–R023/R025 would change to Heavy; if Bidder 3 was judged to have submitted a formal indication, its formality would rise [...]\nSTATUS: Pending\n====================================================================================================\nQ5 | Inferred closing-out of participants (9 non-submitting NDA signers at the 10/30/2014 solicitation)\nRECOMMENDED: Keep one inferred residual row (R024): 15 NDA signers − 6 submitters = 9 non-submitters, Outcome basis Inferred: residual, Decided by Unknown, Exit reason Not stated, Count 9, Working date = the 10/30/2014 due date. All other close-outs are stated: 2 dropped (R027), Bidder 3 did not submit (R038), Bidder 2 not selected at signing (R046); the winner has no exit row.\nWHY: Base: 15 signers and the October IOI instruction (P-013, P-014); submitters: six (P-016). The arithmetic assumes every signer was eligible to submit and the six exhaust the submissions; non-submission at this solicitation is not permanent withdrawal and does not reveal identity or motive. Two strategic contacts never entered and need no close-out.\nAFFECTED: R024 (inferred row); related tallies on R017, R020–R023; balance shown in Summary\nCONSEQUENCE: If a non-submitter had actually advanced to the final round by an oral indication, the residual would still count 9 non-submissions at the written IOI step, but the four-finalist composition reading in Q2 would shift; if some signers were not invited to submit, the base would be smaller and [...]\nSTATUS: Pending\n====================================================================================================\nQ6 | Deadlines and working-date conventions (12/05 superseded; 12/10 Extended; 12/12 Enforced; assigned dates deciding order)\nRECOMMENDED: Keep the deadline history as extracted: 12/05/2014 initial date set (R032, superseded before arrival; no milestone row), revised 12/04–05 to 12/10 (R033) so R034 reads Extended, improved bids due 12/12 (R039) with R040 Enforced. Keep assigned Working dates that decide in-round order where days are undisclosed (R025 midpoint 10/31; R029/R030 November midpoint 11/15; R028 first day after selection 11/04; R018 midpoint 10/15; R024 due date 10/30).\nWHY: Deadline facts: P-020 (initial 12/15 completion and 12/05 submissions), P-021 (12/10 set), P-026 (12/12 request). Treatment decisions follow the instruction rules and what followed in each round (board selection 11/03; board approval 12/13). Assigned dates are disclosed conventions, not observed dates.\nAFFECTED: R018, R019, R024, R025, R028–R034, R040; Date basis/method fields on those rows\nCONSEQUENCE: Changing treatments would alter the Summary deadline map (e.g., reading 12/10 as Enforced if the 12/12 request is not treated as its extension). Moving assigned dates may reorder rows within the round; Row ids and quotes would need re-sorting.\nSTATUS: Pending\n====================================================================================================\nQ7 | Advisers and conflicts (J.P. Morgan; Wachtell Lipton; Innisfree; buyer-side advisers)\nRECOMMENDED: Keep J.P. Morgan as the target's financial adviser with the disclosed conflict facts in the row (fee up to ~$39 million, substantially contingent; ~$110 million of Buyer Group relationships over two years; James Crown's Longview/JPMorgan Chase connection). Keep Wachtell Lipton as service observed with the retention date undisclosed. Keep Innisfree as a disclosed proxy-solicitation adviser. Buyer-side advisers: not disclosed.\nWHY: P-005, X-025, X-029, X-030 (relationships), X-018, P-004. The filing discloses the relationships itself; no outside knowledge is used.\nAFFECTED: R004, R005, R049; Summary adviser block\nCONSEQUENCE: If reviewers prefer strict adviser-only rows, Innisfree moves to Summary; J.P. Morgan conflict facts would remain because the filing makes them material to the fairness opinion and the board's process.\nSTATUS: Pending\n======================================================================