{"type":"text","timestamp":1789825287523,"sessionID":"ses_f46293c76ffe0Qb4SRXqQEDupS","part":{"id":"prt_0b9e665f6001nqbrO014Vn9QuH_text-0","sessionID":"ses_f46293c76ffe0Qb4SRXqQEDupS","messageID":"msg_0b9e665f6001nqbrO014Vn9QuH","type":"text","text":"The workbook is complete and verified. Final deliverable:\n\n**`/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/petsmart.xlsx`** — four visible sheets (Deal ledger, Summary, Questions, Source text) plus the hidden Lists sheet, built from `raw_filing/petsmart_2015-02-02_DEFM14A.htm` (PetSmart DEFM14A, filed 02/02/2015) under the short-form instruction of 19 September 2026. 49 ledger rows; 69 source-text rows (P-001…P-031 background; X-001…X-038 other passages); 15 controlled drop-downs with defined-name lists; row-level local links from each ledger Source cell to its main source paragraph; six SUMIFS tally formulas in Summary.\n\n## The sale, in short\n\nPetSmart began 2014 reviewing alternatives (including buying a privately-held \"Industry Participant\") and, after weak Q1 results, faced JANA Partners' 13D (9.9%, 07/03/2014) and Longview's public sale advocacy (07/07/2014). On 08/13/2014 the board decided to explore a sale, announced it 08/19, and had J.P. Morgan work the market: 27 parties contacted, 15 financial buyers signed confidentiality/standstill agreements in early October, and six submitted non-binding IOIs on 10/30/2014 ($78–$85 ranges). On 11/03 the board advanced the four bidders at/above $80 to a final round; two of them combined into \"Bidder 3\". The 12/10 final bids were $80.70 (Buyer Group) and $80.35 (Bidder 2), with Bidder 3 dropping out at a valuation ≤ ~$78; after the target demanded improvements, Bidder 2 gave a best-and-final $81.50 and the BC Partners-led Buyer Group $83.00 in cash. The board approved the Buyer Group on 12/13 and the merger was signed and announced 12/14/2014 at $83.00 per share, with Longview rolling over 3,012,050 shares (~$250M) into Parent and voting its 7,424,591 shares for the deal. No competing proposal is reported as of the proxy, and no closing is observed — completion was expected in the first half of 2015 (end date 06/14/2015).\n\n## Most consequential review items (all Pending in the workbook)\n\n- **Q1 — Round map.** One process; Round 1 anchored on the confidentiality wave (rejected candidates Aug 13, Aug 19, Oct 3, and the 27-contact aggregate kept as separate rows); Round 3 split from Round 2 on the November first request for final bids (alternative: a two-round map).\n- **Q2 — Counts/identities.** Six IOI submitters vs the filing's \"5 bidder groups\"; \"four bidders ≥$80\" vs three described ranges — recommended reading: the four are the Buyer Group, Bidder 2 and the two later Bidder 3 members, with the residual cohort carrying the unnamed units; no identity backfill.\n- **Q4 — Formality/conditions.** IOIs Informal with Conditions \"Insufficient evidence\"; December bids Formal/Light; Bidder 3's ≤ ~$78 indication recorded as a Bound-only ceiling, Informal.\n- **Q5 — Inferred close-out.** One inferred residual row: 15 signers − 6 submitters = 9 non-submitters at the 10/30 deadline; every other close-out is stated (2 dropped, Bidder 3 did not submit, Bidder 2 not selected at signing; the winner has no exit row).\n- **Q6 — Deadlines.** 12/05 set-then-superseded (no milestone row); 12/10 Extended; 12/12 Enforced; assigned Working dates (midpoints/bounds) decide in-round order where days are undisclosed.\n- **Q7 — Advisers.** J.P. Morgan's ~$39M contingent fee and ~$110M Buyer Group relationships; Wachtell retention date undisclosed; Innisfree included; buyer-side advisers not disclosed.\n- **Q8 — Coverage conventions.** Industry Participant kept as context (never entered, never closed); rollover communication folded into the October deadline row; regulatory/litigation only as Summary lines; no go-shop.\n\n## What I could not verify\n\n- **Formula evaluation in a spreadsheet app:** LibreOffice crashes in this sandbox on any file, so I recomputed the SUMIFS logic in Python (27 contacts, 15 NDAs, 6 round-1 bids, 3 round-3 bids, 10/2/1 outcomes). No cached values are stored, so Excel/LibreOffice should compute them on open.\n- **Visual rendering:** column-group collapse controls, wrapping/widths and filter appearance were written correctly per openpyxl but not opened in a GUI; the \"Reviewer note\" column is empty as required.\n- **Conventions flagged, not facts:** every assigned Working date, the round boundaries and the anonymous-bidder/cohort treatments are analytical conventions — documented in the rows, Summary and Questions, and the quotes are all recoverable from the Source text sheet.","time":{"start":1789825279488,"end":1789825287523}}}
